{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680211755,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db46c49e001i1kjm8H1YqnkWU","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db468a6d001dPiVaT3q9Mf0Bo","type":"tool","id":"call_6440af0abc73443c9d14d88d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-4b.txt"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-4b.txt, lines 1-19\n1: # confirming round of review pass four: git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --name-only 11af224a34 48f03b5013 -- .skilled .opencode (row files excluded)\n2: # area<TAB>path; lineage scorer-attach-confirm-4b reviews area scorer-attach, accuracy-runner-confirm-4b reviews area accuracy-runner\n3: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n4: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\n5: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\n6: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\n7: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n8: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n9: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n10: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\n11: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n12: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\n13: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n14: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\n15: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n16: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n17: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\n18: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n19: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-4b.txt, lines 1-19\n1: # confirming round of review pass four: git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --name-only 11af224a34 48f03b5013 -- .skilled .opencode (row files excluded)\n2: # area<TAB>path; lineage scorer-attach-confirm-4b reviews area scorer-attach, accuracy-runner-confirm-4b reviews area accuracy-runner\n3: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n4: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\n5: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\n6: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\n7: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n8: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n9: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n10: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\n11: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n12: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\n13: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n14: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\n15: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n16: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n17: accuracy-runner\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\n18: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n19: scorer-attach\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-4b.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680210590,"end":1794680211755}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680211758,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db46c5b6001VntVwpqLksdist","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db468a6d001dPiVaT3q9Mf0Bo","type":"tool","id":"call_b1b061c5b3e34290bee70ecb","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md, lines 1-31\n1: # Review pass four, verification of findings\n2: \n3: Verifier: Opus 5.5 high, 2026-11-14, read-only on code. Probes in `probes/`. The holdout rule held: command-prompts.jsonl was only read through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`.\n4: \n5: Count: confirmed P0 0, P1 3, P2 15. Rejected 3.\n6: \n7: - SA4-P1-002: CONFIRMED P1. A refusal over \"A or B\" keeps the second command. `do not run /create:agent or /create:readme` gives `/create:readme (start)` on the top row; `never use /create:readme or /create:feature-catalog` gives `/create:feature-catalog (start)`; `do not run /deep:review, or /deep:research` gives `/deep:research (ask)`. Fix: carry a refusal over or-lists in `commandOnlyMentioned` (command-attach.ts).\n8: - SA4-P1-001: CONFIRMED, accepted limit, P2 (020 spec.md:242, T017). Retired name typed in a refusal.\n9: - SA4-P1-003: CONFIRMED, deliberate tradeoff, P2 (020 T021, T024, P017). Broad creation words.\n10: - SA4-P2-001: CONFIRMED P2. Add `(?:the )?` to `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD`; the question also puts `/doctor:update (ask)` on the top row.\n11: - SA4-P2-002: CONFIRMED P2. advisor-recommend.md:39, the lead row keeps its command.\n12: - SA4-P2-003: CONFIRMED P2. command-meaning-matching.md:65, 17 becomes 28.\n13: - SA4-P2-004: CONFIRMED P2. Phase 020 spec.md:122, :184 and AC-007 say 10, the code uses 9.\n14: - SA4-P2-005: CONFIRMED P2. Add a test row with each root fix.\n15: - R4-P2-001: CONFIRMED P2. codex.mjs:167 opens the caller's locator after containment resolved another path (symlink swap probe). Read `storePath`; keep `recordedSessionId` on `transcriptPath`.\n16: - R4-P2-002: REJECTED. The first returned row always leads (fusion.ts:1617-1618; 0 of 195 labeled and 0 of 78 doctor rows differ).\n17: - R4-P2-003: CONFIRMED P2. README:121 should name `parent-named only`.\n18: - iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted: CONFIRMED P1. `offeredAs` is dropped by `backfillRunLog` (shown by run) and by `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187` (by reading). A partner-side command then counts as an offer.\n19: - iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated: REJECTED. A move from 8 to 9 already fails the suite (slice test compares the whole block); the 8 of 24 is accepted by P041.\n20: - iter1-P2-heredoc-delimiter: CONFIRMED P2. End markers with `-` or `.` are read as commands; no stored number moves.\n21: - iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start: CONFIRMED, raised to P1. A shell `cat` of a command document then a write gives `started:false`. A scorer copy accepting shell reads moves 7 of 12 stored start lines (codex pre 0 to 1 of 12, codex post 0 to 1, pi pre 0 to 3 of 11, dsh post 6 to 9 of 12). `takenLoop` misses such loops, and phase 026 T024 builds on `readDocument`.\n22: - iter2-P2-live-holdout-guard-baseline-only: CONFIRMED P2. Check the live capture too.\n23: - iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned: REJECTED. command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:277-280 compares the whole block.\n24: - iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows: CONFIRMED P2. README: the paired block needs a shared owned row.\n25: - iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision: CONFIRMED P2 (hand-written logs only). Reserve `paired`.\n26: - iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field: CONFIRMED P2. Delete the field.\n27: - DR4-P2-001: CONFIRMED P2. The A11 row should name the by-hand fix for a malformed row.\n28: \n29: Fixes that overlap phase 026: offeredAs and the shell-read start must land before 026 T002 and its sessions. The pair doc, the `paired` name and `unscoredOnly` can fold into 026 T018 and T019.\n30: \n31: Seen outside the 21, not graded: `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` puts `/create:readme (start)` on the top row. `/doctor:deep-loop (run, add-only)` as third row on deep-loop refusals falls under P007.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md, lines 1-31\n1: # Review pass four, verification of findings\n2: \n3: Verifier: Opus 5.5 high, 2026-11-14, read-only on code. Probes in `probes/`. The holdout rule held: command-prompts.jsonl was only read through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`.\n4: \n5: Count: confirmed P0 0, P1 3, P2 15. Rejected 3.\n6: \n7: - SA4-P1-002: CONFIRMED P1. A refusal over \"A or B\" keeps the second command. `do not run /create:agent or /create:readme` gives `/create:readme (start)` on the top row; `never use /create:readme or /create:feature-catalog` gives `/create:feature-catalog (start)`; `do not run /deep:review, or /deep:research` gives `/deep:research (ask)`. Fix: carry a refusal over or-lists in `commandOnlyMentioned` (command-attach.ts).\n8: - SA4-P1-001: CONFIRMED, accepted limit, P2 (020 spec.md:242, T017). Retired name typed in a refusal.\n9: - SA4-P1-003: CONFIRMED, deliberate tradeoff, P2 (020 T021, T024, P017). Broad creation words.\n10: - SA4-P2-001: CONFIRMED P2. Add `(?:the )?` to `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD`; the question also puts `/doctor:update (ask)` on the top row.\n11: - SA4-P2-002: CONFIRMED P2. advisor-recommend.md:39, the lead row keeps its command.\n12: - SA4-P2-003: CONFIRMED P2. command-meaning-matching.md:65, 17 becomes 28.\n13: - SA4-P2-004: CONFIRMED P2. Phase 020 spec.md:122, :184 and AC-007 say 10, the code uses 9.\n14: - SA4-P2-005: CONFIRMED P2. Add a test row with each root fix.\n15: - R4-P2-001: CONFIRMED P2. codex.mjs:167 opens the caller's locator after containment resolved another path (sy