kill_agent\":{\"level\":\"overlay\",\"notes\":\"No agent definition changed in this area.\",\"status\":\"notApplicable\"},\"spec_code\":{\"level\":\"core\",\"notes\":\"One active P1 (coordinated refusal); two accepted limits are P2s; REQ-007 text is stale.\",\"status\":\"partial\"}},\"type\":\"iteration\"}\n{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"synthesis_complete\",\"stem\":\"deep_review.synthesis_complete\",\"runId\":\"scorer-attach-4\",\"sessionId\":\"scorer-attach-4\",\"activeP0\":0,\"activeP1\":1,\"activeP2\":7,\"dimensionCoverage\":1,\"mode\":\"review\",\"releaseReadinessState\":\"in-progress\",\"stopReason\":\"maxIterationsReached\",\"totalIterations\":4,\"verdict\":\"CONDITIONAL\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-14T15:42:15.757Z\"}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"Review: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\",\"maxIterations\":4,\"generation\":1,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-14T15:29:09.038Z\"}\n{\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"dimensions\":[\"correctness\"],\"durationMs\":420000,\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-522\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:860-960,1120-1260,1580-1620\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:429-514,620-710\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-56,135-432\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:155-190,382-482\"],\"findingDetails\":[{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"typed-command attach\",\"retired-command map\",\"/create:sk-skill start policy\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The retired name could be treated as a distinct command, but the map's comment says it reads as the replacement, so the guards should agree.\",\"claim\":\"A refusal written with the retired command name still attaches the live command because the retired-name rewrite runs before the mention guard.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The compiled route for the same prompt returns defer, so the typed path is the live caller; the probe confirms the top row is sk-doc.\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if the retired name is deliberately excluded from the live command's refusal semantics.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:240\",\"command-attach.ts:256\",\"handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:500\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"findingClass\":\"guard_gap\",\"id\":\"SA4-P1-001\",\"iteration\":1,\"scopeProof\":\"command-attach.ts and handlers/advisor-recommend.ts are in the declared scorer-attach scope; the handler is the only production caller of typedCommandForTop.\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"A refusal typed with the retired command name still delivers the live mutating command\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"typed-command attach\",\"multi-command refusals\",\"/deep:research ask policy\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The reader may have refused only the first command and merely named the second, but 'do not run A or B' refuses both.\",\"claim\":\"A refusal that coordinates two command names attaches the second one because the mention reader requires a separate lead before each occurrence.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The compiled route returns defer and the scorer top is system-deep-loop; a single-command refusal is correctly withheld, so the gap is the coordinated form.\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if a coordinated refusal is judged a mention of both commands rather than a refusal of both.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:414\",\"command-attach.ts:419\",\"command-attach.ts:360\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"findingClass\":\"guard_gap\",\"id\":\"SA4-P1-002\",\"iteration\":1,\"scopeProof\":\"The prompt is an ordinary refusal of two tracked commands; the typed path and handler are in scope, and no other module rewrites the lead.\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"A coordinated refusal names the second command without a lead, so the typed path still delivers it\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"small-edit gate\",\"/create:readme start policy\",\"correction prompts with verification clauses\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"'new' or 'make sure' could be read as a request to author a fresh document, but the sentence's verb is fix and the object is an existing readme.\",\"claim\":\"The small-edit gate treats generic creation words inside a correction clause as a request to create the whole document, so a correction prompt still receives /create:readme.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The two REQ-004 control prompts return no command, and the phase Out of Scope excludes edits with no correction word; these prompts name a typo or grammar error.\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if the creation-request guard is intentionally broad and these clauses are judged outside the correction class.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:331\",\"command-attach.ts:487\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:487\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"findingClass\":\"guard_gap\",\"id\":\"SA4-P1-003\",\"iteration\":1,\"scopeProof\":\"All four prompts are correction requests inside an existing readme; the compiled route for the sk-doc hub and the attach function are the declared target.\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"A correction inside one document still attaches the creation workflow when the sentence carries a generic creation word\"}],\"findingsCount\":3,\"findingsNew\":[\"SA4-P1-001\",\"SA4-P1-002\",\"SA4-P1-003\"],\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":3,\"P2\":0},\"focus\":\"correctness\",\"generation\":1,\"iteration\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"mod