{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680293269,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db48004c0024xU6eBX0VYm4be","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db47e30d001IFqCUKBiq63MQ8","type":"tool","id":"call_b9700cec006d4520ad4991ca","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 11af224a34 48f03b5013 -- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\nindex b08fe38e6e..c3ea25ad04 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@ A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n | `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n | `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n | `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n+| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |\n | `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n | The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n | The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\nindex 9d082de0e5..492e6ca560 100644\n--- a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\n+++ b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n-{\"version\":3,\"file\":\"codex.d.mts\",\"sourceRoot\":\"\",\"sources\":[\"codex.mjs\"],\"names\":[],\"mappings\":\"AAyCA,kDAGC;AAiGD;;;;;;;;;;;;;EAkDC\"}\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+{\"version\":3,\"file\":\"codex.d.mts\",\"sourceRoot\":\"\",\"sources\":[\"codex.mjs\"],\"names\":[],\"mappings\":\"AAyCA,kDAGC;AAiGD;;;;;;;;;;;;;EAoDC\"}\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\nindex ce949e957c..11f71a1115 100644\n--- a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\n@@ -164,7 +164,9 @@ export function loadCodexSession({ sessionId, transcriptPath, ...options } = {})\n \n   let raw;\n   try {\n-    raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');\n+    // The read is the file containment resolved, so a path repointed after the\n+    // check is not read in its place.\n+    raw = readFileSync(storePath, 'utf8');\n   } catch {\n     try {\n       statSync(root);\ndiff --git a/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs b/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\nindex 0fb0fd15b4..f2a8fc81a8 100644\n--- a/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@\n // borrows another runtime's store.\n \n import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import { realpathSync, symlinkSync } from 'node:fs';\n import { join } from 'node:path';\n import { test } from 'node:test';\n \n@@ -99,6 +100,37 @@ test('a rollout outside the store is refused without reading it', async () => {\n   });\n });\n \n+test('a rollout reached through a link inside the store is read at the resolved path', async () => {\n+  await withTempAsync('codex-link', async (root) => {\n+    const fixture = codexSession({ root });\n+    const link = join(fixture.root, 'link.jsonl');\n+    symlinkSync(fixture.filePath, link);\n+\n+    const tracker = trackFileOpens();\n+    try {\n+      const result = await loadSession({\n+        runtime: 'codex',\n+        sessionId: SESSION,\n+        codexRoot: fixture.root,\n+        transcriptPath: link,\n+      });\n+      assert.equal(result.ok, true);\n+      assert.equal(\n+        tracker.opened.includes(link),\n+        false,\n+        `the link path was opened: ${tracker.opened.join(', ')}`,\n+      );\n+      assert.equal(\n+        tracker.opened.includes(realpathSync(fixture.filePath)),\n+        true,\n+        `the resolved file was not opened: ${tracker.opened.join(', ')}`,\n+      );\n+    } finally {\n+      tracker.restore();\n+    }\n+  });\n+});\n+\n test('the header id wins over a rollout file name that disagrees', () => {\n   withTemp('codex-header-wins', (root) => {\n     const fixture = codexSession({ root, fileName: `rollout-2026-11-07T12-00-00-${DECOY}.jsonl` });\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\nindex 36dab643bb..c18be338c6 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -62,10 +62,11 @@ Run individual scripts from the repository root with the documented arguments.\n \n ### Attribution on every run line\n \n-Each line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n+Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n \n - `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n - `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n+- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.\n - `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a readable record, and `unknown` where none exists or cannot be read, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n \n The offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n@@ -119,7 +120,7 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `score-routing-corpus.py` | PY source file in this folder. |\n | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt corpus with a gold slash command per row, covering every tracked command. |\n | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Three of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 5 of 8. |\n-| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n | `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n@@ -184,7 +185,7 @@ node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-c\n   --backfill scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --out scratch/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl\n ```\n \n-The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n+The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n \n ---\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\nindex 37f9f1bd88..432522e885 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ import { join } from 'node:path';\n import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\n import { afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n-import { G2_ROWS, armFor, childEnv, lineFixture, liveArmRefusal } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs';\n+import { G2_ROWS, armFor, childEnv, lineFixture, liveArmRefusal, offerLineFields } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs';\n import { startedLabel } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs';\n \n describe('childEnv', () => {\n@@ -107,6 +107,25 @@ describe('lineFixture', () => {\n   });\n });\n \n+describe('offerLineFields', () => {\n+  it('copies the offered command, its policy and where it sat', () => {\n+    expect(\n+      offerLineFields({\n+        offeredCommand: '/create:readme',\n+        offeredPolicy: 'start',\n+        offeredAs: 'partner',\n+        offerError: null,\n+      }),\n+    ).toEqual({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' });\n+  });\n+\n+  it('writes null where the replay found no offer', () => {\n+    expect(\n+      offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }),\n+    ).toEqual({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null });\n+  });\n+});\n+\n describe('liveArmRefusal', () => {\n   const dirs: string[] = [];\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\nindex 79cb77268e..fd5e74ee98 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\n@@ -355,6 +355,42 @@ describe('backfillRunLog', () => {\n     }\n   });\n \n+  it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head', async () => {\n+    const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'command-offer-'));\n+    const outPath = join(dir, 'runs-out.jsonl');\n+    const inPath = writeRunLog(dir, [\n+      { runtime: 'claude', rowId: 'row-one', arm: 'pre', locator: { projectDir: '/checkout-one' }, exit: 0, changedPaths: [] },\n+      { runtime: 'claude', rowId: 'row-two', arm: 'pre', locator: { projectDir: '/checkout-one' }, exit: 0, changedPaths: [] },\n+    ]);\n+    try {\n+      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n+        inPath,\n+        outPath,\n+        promptFor: (rowId: string) => `prompt for ${rowId}`,\n+        warm: async () => {},\n+        replay: async ({ sessionId }: { checkoutDir: string; prompt: string; sessionId: string }) => (\n+          sessionId === 'backfill-row-one'\n+            ? {\n+              offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook',\n+              offeredPolicy: 'start',\n+              offeredAs: 'partner',\n+              offerError: null,\n+            }\n+            : { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }\n+        ),\n+        brief: async () => true,\n+        trusted: () => true,\n+      });\n+\n+      expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, lines: 2, outPath });\n+      const written = readFileSync(outPath, 'utf8').trim().split('\\n').map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n+      expect(written[0].offeredAs).toBe('partner');\n+      expect(written[1].offeredAs).toBeNull();\n+    } finally {\n+      rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+    }\n+  });\n+\n   it('hands each line to the prompt lookup', async () => {\n     const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'command-offer-'));\n     const outPath = join(dir, 'runs-out.jsonl');\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\nindex b08fe38e6e..c3ea25ad04 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@ A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n | `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n | `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n | `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n+| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |\n | `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n | The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n | The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\nindex 9d082de0e5..492e6ca560 100644\n--- a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\n+++ b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n-{\"version\":3,\"file\":\"codex.d.mts\",\"sourceRoot\":\"\",\"sources\":[\"codex.mjs\"],\"names\":[],\"mappings\":\"AAyCA,kDAGC;AAiGD;;;;;;;;;;;;;EAkDC\"}\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+{\"version\":3,\"file\":\"codex.d.mts\",\"sourceRoot\":\"\",\"sources\":[\"codex.mjs\"],\"names\":[],\"mappings\":\"AAyCA,kDAGC;AAiGD;;;;;;;;;;;;;EAoDC\"}\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\nindex ce949e957c..11f71a1115 100644\n--- a/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs\n@@ -164,7 +164,9 @@ export function loadCodexSession({ sessionId, transcriptPath, ...options } = {})\n \n   let raw;\n   try {\n-    raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');\n+    // The read is the file containment resolved, so a path repointed after the\n+    // check is not read in its place.\n+    raw = readFileSync(storePath, 'utf8');\n   } catch {\n     try {\n       statSync(root);\ndiff --git a/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs b/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\nindex 0fb0fd15b4..f2a8fc81a8 100644\n--- a/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@\n // borrows another runtime's store.\n \n import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+import { realpathSync, symlinkSync } from 'node:fs';\n import { join } from 'node:path';\n import { test } from 'node:test';\n \n@@ -99,6 +100,37 @@ test('a rollout outside the store is refused without reading it', async () => {\n   });\n });\n \n+test('a rollout reached through a link inside the store is read at the resolved path', async () => {\n+  await withTempAsync('codex-link', async (root) => {\n+    const fixture = codexSession({ root });\n+    const link = join(fixture.root, 'link.jsonl');\n+    symlinkSync(fixture.filePath, link);\n+\n+    const tracker = trackFileOpens();\n+    try {\n+      const result = await loadSession({\n+        runtime: 'codex',\n+        sessionId: SESSION,\n+        codexRoot: fixture.root,\n+        transcriptPath: link,\n+      });\n+      assert.equal(result.ok, true);\n+      assert.equal(\n+        tracker.opened.includes(link),\n+        false,\n+        `the link path was opened: ${tracker.opened.join(', ')}`,\n+      );\n+      assert.equal(\n+        tracker.opened.includes(realpathSync(fixture.filePath)),\n+        true,\n+        `the resolved file was not opened: ${tracker.opened.join(', ')}`,\n+      );\n+    } finally {\n+      tracker.restore();\n+    }\n+  });\n+});\n+\n test('the header id wins over a rollout file name that disagrees', () => {\n   withTemp('codex-header-wins', (root) => {\n     const fixture = codexSession({ root, fileName: `rollout-2026-11-07T12-00-00-${DECOY}.jsonl` });\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\nindex 36dab643bb..c18be338c6 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -62,10 +62,11 @@ Run individual scripts from the repository root with the documented arguments.\n \n ### Attribution on every run line\n \n-Each line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n+Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n \n - `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n - `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n+- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.\n - `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a readable record, and `unknown` where none exists or cannot be read, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n \n The offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n@@ -119,7 +120,7 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `score-routing-corpus.py` | PY source file in this folder. |\n | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt corpus with a gold slash command per row, covering every tracked command. |\n | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Three of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 5 of 8. |\n-| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n | `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n@@ -184,7 +185,7 @@ node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-c\n   --backfill scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --out scratch/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl\n ```\n \n-The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n+The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n \n ---\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\nindex 37f9f1bd88..432522e885 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ import { join } from 'node:path';\n import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\n import { afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n-import { G2_ROWS, armFor, childEnv, lineFixture, liveArmRefusal } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs';\n+import { G2_ROWS, armFor, childEnv, lineFixture, liveArmRefusal, offerLineFields } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs';\n import { startedLabel } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs';\n \n describe('childEnv', () => {\n@@ -107,6 +107,25 @@ describe('lineFixture', () => {\n   });\n });\n \n+describe('offerLineFields', () => {\n+  it('copies the offered command, its policy and where it sat', () => {\n+    expect(\n+      offerLineFields({\n+        offeredCommand: '/create:readme',\n+        offeredPolicy: 'start',\n+        offeredAs: 'partner',\n+        offerError: null,\n+      }),\n+    ).toEqual({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' });\n+  });\n+\n+  it('writes null where the replay found no offer', () => {\n+    expect(\n+      offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }),\n+    ).toEqual({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null });\n+  });\n+});\n+\n describe('liveArmRefusal', () => {\n   const dirs: string[] = [];\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\nindex 79cb77268e..fd5e74ee98 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\n@@ -355,6 +355,42 @@ describe('backfillRunLog', () => {\n     }\n   });\n \n+  it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head', async () => {\n+    const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'command-offer-'));\n+    const outPath = join(dir, 'runs-out.jsonl');\n+    const inPath = writeRunLog(dir, [\n+      { runtime: 'claude', rowId: 'row-one', arm: 'pre', locator: { projectDir: '/checkout-one' }, exit: 0, changedPaths: [] },\n+      { runtime: 'claude', rowId: 'row-two', arm: 'pre', locator: { projectDir: '/checkout-one' }, exit: 0, changedPaths: [] },\n+    ]);\n+    try {\n+      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n+        inPath,\n+        outPath,\n+        promptFor: (rowId: string) => `prompt for ${rowId}`,\n+        warm: async () => {},\n+        replay: async ({ sessionId }: { checkoutDir: string; prompt: string; sessionId: string }) => (\n+          sessionId === 'backfill-row-one'\n+            ? {\n+              offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook',\n+              offeredPolicy: 'start',\n+              offeredAs: 'partner',\n+              offerError: null,\n+            }\n+            : { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }\n+        ),\n+        brief: async () => true,\n+        trusted: () => true,\n+      });\n+\n+      expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, lines: 2, outPath });\n+      const written = readFileSync(outPath, 'utf8').trim().split('\\n').map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n+      expect(written[0].offeredAs).toBe('partner');\n+      expect(written[1].offeredAs).toBeNull();\n+    } finally {\n+      rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+    }\n+  });\n+\n   it('hands each line to the prompt lookup', async () => {\n     const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'command-offer-'));\n     const outPath = join(dir, 'runs-out.jsonl');\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 11af224a34 48f03b5013 -- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.d.mts.map .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680291404,"end":1794680293269}}}}
