ll-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:623:// A row is read one line at a time so a holdout row is refused before its prompt\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:633:    if (row.split === 'holdout') {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:634:      throw new Refusal('holdout_row', `${rowId}: a holdout row is never run`);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1201:// is joined to its row before a transcript is read. A holdout row is marked and\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1220:    holdout: false,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1236:    labels.set(row.id, row.split === 'holdout' ? { holdout: true } : rowLabel(row));\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1301:    holdout: false,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1510:  if (label.holdout) return { scored: false, reason: 'holdout_row' };\n=== live capture refs ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:89:`capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` reports typed reach twice under `attachedMetrics`:\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:122:| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. Its `attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor` counts the silent rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)`, and `needsModeRows` lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it. `attachedMetrics.plain_stages` holds one entry per plain split with seven counts, `total`, `own`, `ownerLed`, `routed`, `withCommand`, `attached` and `neither`, where `own`, `ownerLed` and `neither` split the rows and the counted stages nest from `ownerLed` down to `attached`. `attachedMetrics.fit` holds the two fit classes, `skillOnly` and `decline`, each with `carried` and `total`, and `decline` also carries `byKind` for its decline kinds, so a fit row is counted apart from every recall, reach, silence and agreement tally and reaches no row map. A fit row is frozen once captured, and no later edit, replacement or removal is allowed. Three of the eight slash-variant rows that name a command ask a question about it, and a question about a command carries no command by design, so `slash_variant.reached_top3` can reach 5 of 8. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:36://   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs            # print JSON to stdout\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:37://   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write    # also write the baseline\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:38://   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding   # score live vectors\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:803:    process.stderr.write('capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs: --write cannot be combined with --real-embedding; the committed baseline is captured under the fixture regime only\\n');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:816:    process.stderr.write(`capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs: ${error.message}\\n`);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:19:} from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:25:const RECAPTURE = 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:132:// The live capture is what the next recapture writes, so a holdout id it\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:209:      `the live capture publishes a per-row outcome for ${publishedLive.length} holdout ids`,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advi