{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680385643,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db496e15001NpbSyQRwTIMMwk","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db493415001p0zitWUlR3YTLR","type":"tool","id":"call_f3682e5b63f34537ba6b65c3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '245,285p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt; echo \"=== header/table above ===\"; sed -n '215,245p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt"},"output":"\n```text\nDOCTOR TARGET FAILED\nTarget: [check|embed|restore]\nStep: [the phase or row that stopped the run]\nError: [the engine's code and message]\nChanged: [what was written before the failure, or none]\nNext: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n```\n\nA check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n\n## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n\n| Situation | Suggested Action |\n|-----------|------------------|\n| A check row reports `FINDING` | Read that row's detail, fix that one requirement, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` |\n| A check row reports `UNKNOWN` | The row could not be answered, not failed. Rerun when its precondition is back, and never report an `UNKNOWN` row as a pass |\n| `A1` reports `stale`, `forked` or `foreign` | `/doctor:agents-md embed` shows what the run would compose and what it would carry before anything is written |\n| `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n| `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n| `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |\n| `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n| The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n| The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\n| The apply reports a dropped line | The engine restored from the backup by itself. Read the dropped line, keep it in the block or in a reference document, then rerun the plan |\n| The embed is not wanted after all | `/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<the backup folder the apply printed>` puts back the files that run wrote |\n| A restore reports a hash that does not match | The record or one of its copies changed, so nothing was written. Read the message. The backup at that directory is kept |\n| A restore reports that the record names another root | The record belongs to the folder it names, and nothing was written. Rerun the restore with `--root <the root the record names>`, in the spaced form: `--root=` is not accepted |\n| Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n\n## 8. Next Step\n\n| Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n|-----------|-------------------|--------|\n| A check row still reports `FINDING` after an embed | `/doctor:agents-md check` | The write is complete, and the remaining row is a different requirement |\n| The composed document is past the byte ceiling | `/doctor:agents-md check` | A6 names the ceiling and what the run kept anyway |\n| The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n| The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n=== header/table above ===\nDeclined: [the embed | the restore]\nChanged: none\nSTATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled\n```\n\n### Dry Run\n\n```text\nDOCTOR DRY RUN\nTarget: [embed|restore]\nPlan: [the engine's plan lines, quoted as printed]\nDry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked.\nChanged: none\nSTATUS=OK\n```\n\n### Restored\n\n```text\nDOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\nTarget: restore\nRun directory: [the --run directory]\nPut back: [each path the restore printed as restored, or none]\nRemoved: [each path it printed as removed, or none]\nFolders: [each folder it printed as removed, or none]\nRe-read: [the check engine's result line]\nSTATUS=OK\n```\n\n### Failure Summary\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n```text\nDOCTOR TARGET FAILED\nTarget: [check|embed|restore]\nStep: [the phase or row that stopped the run]\nError: [the engine's code and message]\nChanged: [what was written before the failure, or none]\nNext: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n```\n\nA check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n\n## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n\n| Situation | Suggested Action |\n|-----------|------------------|\n| A check row reports `FINDING` | Read that row's detail, fix that one requirement, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` |\n| A check row reports `UNKNOWN` | The row could not be answered, not failed. Rerun when its precondition is back, and never report an `UNKNOWN` row as a pass |\n| `A1` reports `stale`, `forked` or `foreign` | `/doctor:agents-md embed` shows what the run would compose and what it would carry before anything is written |\n| `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n| `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n| `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |\n| `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n| The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n| The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\n| The apply reports a dropped line | The engine restored from the backup by itself. Read the dropped line, keep it in the block or in a reference document, then rerun the plan |\n| The embed is not wanted after all | `/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<the backup folder the apply printed>` puts back the files that run wrote |\n| A restore reports a hash that does not match | The record or one of its copies changed, so nothing was written. Read the message. The backup at that directory is kept |\n| A restore reports that the record names another root | The record belongs to the folder it names, and nothing was written. Rerun the restore with `--root <the root the record names>`, in the spaced form: `--root=` is not accepted |\n| Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n\n## 8. Next Step\n\n| Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n|-----------|-------------------|--------|\n| A check row still reports `FINDING` after an embed | `/doctor:agents-md check` | The write is complete, and the remaining row is a different requirement |\n| The composed document is past the byte ceiling | `/doctor:agents-md check` | A6 names the ceiling and what the run kept anyway |\n| The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n| The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n=== header/table above ===\nDeclined: [the embed | the restore]\nChanged: none\nSTATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled\n```\n\n### Dry Run\n\n```text\nDOCTOR DRY RUN\nTarget: [embed|restore]\nPlan: [the engine's plan lines, quoted as printed]\nDry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked.\nChanged: none\nSTATUS=OK\n```\n\n### Restored\n\n```text\nDOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\nTarget: restore\nRun directory: [the --run directory]\nPut back: [each path the restore printed as restored, or none]\nRemoved: [each path it printed as removed, or none]\nFolders: [each folder it printed as removed, or none]\nRe-read: [the check engine's result line]\nSTATUS=OK\n```\n\n### Failure Summary\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '245,285p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt; echo \\\"=== header/table above ===\\\"; sed -n '215,245p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680385045,"end":1794680385643}}}}
