 to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n124:| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n188:The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"three fields\\\\|those three\\\\|four fields\\\\|offeredAs\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680465911,"end":1794680466397}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680466404,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db4aa6990016Z12indsE16ZDp","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db4a691d001UH322X6Bq1oSn2","type":"tool","id":"call_e6c6e1ffb9a24710ae4375ce","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"function offerOf\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs; sed -n \"$(grep -n 'function offerOf' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | cut -d: -f1),+55p\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs"},"output":"1468:function offerOf(line, label) {\nfunction offerOf(line, label) {\n  const hasOffer = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(line, 'offeredCommand');\n  const wanted = commandParts(label.expected_command);\n  return {\n    offered: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n    partner: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n    offerFieldAbsent: !hasOffer,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Score one run log line against the row its turn answered.\n *\n * A run is scored whenever its session loads, whatever exit the turn ended with.\n * The exit code never decides a score, because a turn the cap stopped still did\n * the work its transcript records, so the code only marks a run as capped.\n *\n * A run that cannot be scored is never dropped: it comes back with the one reason\n * the summary counts apart from its denominators, so an arm that produced no\n * transcript reads as unscored rather than as a rate over the runs that survived.\n *\n * @param {object} line - One line of a run log.\n * @param {Map<string, object>} labels - The corpus labels, keyed by row id.\n * @param {{byCommand: Map<string, string>, skills: Set<string>}} owners - The\n *   command to skill table and the set of known skills.\n * @returns {Promise<{scored: false, reason: string}\n *   | {scored: true, capped: boolean, startRow: boolean, started: boolean,\n *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offeredAsPartner: boolean,\n *      offerSeen: boolean,\n *      commandState: string|null, briefDelivered: boolean|'unknown',\n *      wrote: boolean, policy: string|null, unsafe: boolean, commandLines: number,\n *      repeated: number, loop: boolean|null,\n *      workflowPath: 'command'|'skill'|'improvised'|'none'|'noOwner'}>}\n */\nasync function scoreRun(line, labels, owners) {\n  const rowId = rowIdOf(line);\n  if (rowId === null) return { scored: false, reason: 'no_row_id' };\n\n  const label = labelFor(rowId, labels);\n  if (label === null) return { scored: false, reason: 'unknown_row' };\n  if (label.holdout) return { scored: false, reason: 'holdout_row' };\n\n  // A turn the cap stopped exits 143, and a turn killed before it wrote an exit\n  // records none. Both left a transcript worth reading, so the code is kept as a\n  // fact about the run rather than as a ground to discard it.\n  const capped = line.exit === 143 || line.exit === null;\n\n  const loaded = await loadSession({ ...locatorOf(line), runtime: line.runtime });\n  if (!loaded.ok) return { scored: false, reason: loaded.code };\n\n  let events;\n  try {\n    events = normalize(loaded.records, line.runtime);\n  } catch {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1468:function offerOf(line, label) {\nfunction offerOf(line, label) {\n  const hasOffer = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(line, 'offeredCommand');\n  const wanted = commandParts(label.expected_command);\n  return {\n    offered: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n    partner: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted)\n      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n    offerFieldAbsent: !hasOffer,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Score one run log line against the row its turn answered.\n *\n * A run is scored whenever its session loads, whatever exit the turn ended with.\n * The exit code never decides a score, because a turn the cap stopped still did\n * the work its transcript records, so the code only marks a run as capped.\n *\n * A run that cannot be scored is never dropped: it comes back with the one reason\n * the summary counts apart from its denominators, so an arm that produced no\n * transcript reads as unscored rather than as a rate over the runs that survived.\n *\n * @param {object} line - One line of a run log.\n * @param {Map<string, object>} labels - The corpus labels, keyed by row id.\n * @param {{byCommand: Map<string, string>, skills: Set<string>}} owners - The\n *   command to skill table and the set of known skills.\n * @returns {Promise<{scored: false, reason: string}\n *   | {scored: true, capped: boolean, startRow: boolean, started: boolean,\n *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offeredAsPartner: boolean,\n *      offerSeen: boolean,\n *      commandState: string|null, briefDelivered: boolean|'unknown',\n *      wrote: boolean, policy: string|null, unsafe: boolean, commandLines: number,\n *      repeated: number, loop: boolean|null,\n *      workflowPath: 'command'|'skill'|'improvised'|'none'|'noOwner'}>}\n */\nasync function scoreRun(line, labels, owners) {\n  const rowId = rowIdOf(line);\n  if (rowId === null) return { scored: false, reason: 'no_row_id' };\n\n  const label = labelFor(rowId, labels);\n  if (label === null) return { scored: false, reason: 'unknown_row' };\n  if (label.holdout) return { scored: false, reason: 'holdout_row' };\n\n  // A turn the cap stopped exits 143, and a turn killed before it wrote an exit\n  // records none. Both left a transcript worth reading, so the code is kept as a\n  // fact about the run rather than as a ground to discard it.\n  const capped = line.exit === 143 || line.exit === null;\n\n  const loaded = await loadSession({ ...locatorOf(line), runtime: line.runtime });\n  if (!loaded.ok) return { scored: false, reason: loaded.code };\n\n  let events;\n  try {\n    events = normalize(loaded.records, line.runtime);\n  } catch {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"function offerOf\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs; sed -n \\\"$(grep -n 'function offerOf' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs | cut -d: -f1),+55p\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680465049,"end":1794680466404}}}}
