{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680512442,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db4b5c5d001aMy54mw7kc3Ycs","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db4af97c00150pGdANdL4R6pg","type":"tool","id":"call_acd50caf744148319a934a07","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | sed -n '60,80p;183,190p'; echo \"=== runner table row ===\"; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | sed -n '125p' | cut -c1-400"},"output":"    60\t| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling and type-discipline checks. |\n    61\t| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n    62\t\n    63\t### Attribution on every run line\n    64\t\n    65\tEach line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n    66\t\n    67\t- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n    68\t- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n    69\t- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.\n    70\t- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a readable record, and `unknown` where none exists or cannot be read, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n    71\t\n    72\tThe offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n    73\t\n    74\t### Backfill a finished log\n    75\t\n    76\t`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n    77\t\n    78\t- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n    79\t- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n    80\t\n   183\t```bash\n   184\tnode .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs \\\n   185\t  --backfill scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --out scratch/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl\n   186\t```\n   187\t\n   188\tThe output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n   189\t\n   190\t---\n=== runner table row ===\n   125\t| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command ro\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    60\t| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling and type-discipline checks. |\n    61\t| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n    62\t\n    63\t### Attribution on every run line\n    64\t\n    65\tEach line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n    66\t\n    67\t- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n    68\t- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n    69\t- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.\n    70\t- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a readable record, and `unknown` where none exists or cannot be read, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n    71\t\n    72\tThe offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n    73\t\n    74\t### Backfill a finished log\n    75\t\n    76\t`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n    77\t\n    78\t- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n    79\t- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n    80\t\n   183\t```bash\n   184\tnode .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs \\\n   185\t  --backfill scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --out scratch/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl\n   186\t```\n   187\t\n   188\tThe output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n   189\t\n   190\t---\n=== runner table row ===\n   125\t| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command ro\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | sed -n '60,80p;183,190p'; echo \\\"=== runner table row ===\\\"; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | sed -n '125p' | cut -c1-400\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680511581,"end":1794680512442}}}}
