{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680778121,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db4f3202002R5hs7yy7UJImXK","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db4f1fac001lLfv8k1EvyN60D","type":"tool","id":"call_5a66f03b5f754584a6aae278","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 1\n\n- Mode: review\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`\n- Iteration: 1 of 3\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 read actions)\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4b.txt`, `review-scope-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `steer.md` (absent)\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`, confirming round of pass four.\nThe dispatcher bound the nine `accuracy-runner` paths in `review/review-scope-4b.txt` plus the\nshared docs that describe them, and the fix range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:43-82,390-508`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:807-828,1150-1210`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:355-390`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:107-126`\n\nContext reads outside the finding surface: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1468-1478` (the reader of `offeredAs`).\n\n## Findings - New\n\nNo new correctness finding.\n\nThe confirmed P1 from the verify report is fixed on both writers:\n\n1. `backfillRunLog` copies `offeredAs` beside the command and policy at\n   `command-offer.mjs:496`, after the replay returns it at `command-offer.mjs:80`.\n2. The live turn uses `offerLineFields` at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, which returns the\n   command, policy and side at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:820-827`.\n3. The brief-only branch at `command-offer.mjs:489-490` still copies the line forward, so a\n   legacy line with no `offeredAs` stays without one and is scored as before by\n   `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\n\nNo input now drops the side between the replay and the written line: the two paths that write a\nline are the only writers in the changed area, and both carry it.\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone in this dimension. Two documentation drifts raised by the fix are recorded under\ntraceability in iteration 3 so they stay in their owning dimension.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: partial. The phase 026 T024 claim that a start is read from the same reads a load\n  uses is implemented by `readDocument` calling the same `shellReadTargets` predicate; this\n  iteration confirms the writer half only.\n- `checklist_evidence`: pending. No checklist row in this area is claimed by iteration 1.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: pending. No agent definition changed.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pending, the README drift is scheduled for iteration 3.\n- `playbook_capability`: notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `run-command-behaviour.mjs` imports `replayOffer` from `command-offer.mjs:56` and writes the\n  live line through the local `appendRunLine` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:663-666`).\n- `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1468-1478` reads `offeredAs` and splits a partner-side command\n  out of the offer count. The two writers therefore feed one reader, and that reader is the\n  only consumer of the new field in the changed area.\n- The append gateway recorded the iteration record and the reducer reads its delta; both live\n  under the lineage directory.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A line with no checkout or an untrusted checkout has no offer object with `offeredAs`; the\n  `?? null` at `command-offer.mjs:496` keeps the field present with a null value. The reader\n  treats a present command with a null side as an offer, which is the pre-fix behavior.\n- A brief-only pass does not invent `offeredAs` for a legacy line. That is the documented\n  contract at `command-offer.mjs:403-404`, and the reader's `offeredAs !== 'partner'` test\n  keeps such a line counted as before.\n- A head that names no command takes the `parseOffer` early return at `command-offer.mjs:73-75`,\n  so `offeredAs` is null rather than a stale side.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `parseOffer` returns one of `head`, `partner` or null, and only the side of the first ` vs `\n  before the match decides it (`command-offer.mjs:70-82`).\n- Both writers preserve the field, and neither writes a partner-side command as an offer.\n- The added backfill test asserts `partner` for the first line and null for the second\n  (`command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`).\n- The added helper test pins the field set and the null case\n  (`command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:110-124`).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A missing `offeredAs` on the live writer: ruled out by `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203` and\n  the helper return at `:820-827`.\n- A missing `offeredAs` on the backfill writer: ruled out by `command-offer.mjs:496`.\n- A partner-side command still counted as an offer: ruled out by\n  `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`, which tests the side before counting.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: the Codex reader's resolved-path read, the holdout guard on the live capture path,\n  and the runner's refusal to run holdout rows.\n- Reason: the pass-four brief names both surfaces; iteration 1 covered the offer persistence.\n- Rotation status: first security pass in this lineage.\n- Required evidence: direct reads of `codex.mjs` containment and read, `identity.mjs`\n  `resolveInside`, the Codex test tracker, and the runner's row guard.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 1\\n\\n- Mode: review\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`\\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`\\n- Iteration: 1 of 3\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 read actions)\\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4b.txt`, `review-scope-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `steer.md` (absent)\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`, confirming round of pass four.\\nThe dispatcher bound the nine `accuracy-runner` paths in `review/review-scope-4b.txt` plus the\\nshared docs that describe them, and the fix range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:43-82,390-508`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:807-828,1150-1210`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:355-390`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:107-126`\\n\\nContext reads outside the finding surface: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1468-1478` (the reader of `offeredAs`).\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\nNo new correctness finding.\\n\\nThe confirmed P1 from the verify report is fixed on both writers:\\n\\n1. `backfillRunLog` copies `offeredAs` beside the command and policy at\\n   `command-offer.mjs:496`, after the replay returns it at `command-offer.mjs:80`.\\n2. The live turn uses `offerLineFields` at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203`, which returns the\\n   command, policy and side at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:820-827`.\\n3. The brief-only branch at `command-offer.mjs:489-490` still copies the line forward, so a\\n   legacy line with no `offeredAs` stays without one and is scored as before by\\n   `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\\n\\nNo input now drops the side between the replay and the written line: the two paths that write a\\nline are the only writers in the changed area, and both carry it.\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone in this dimension. Two documentation drifts raised by the fix are recorded under\\ntraceability in iteration 3 so they stay in their owning dimension.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: partial. The phase 026 T024 claim that a start is read from the same reads a load\\n  uses is implemented by `readDocument` calling the same `shellReadTargets` predicate; this\\n  iteration confirms the writer half only.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: pending. No checklist row in this area is claimed by iteration 1.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: pending. No agent definition changed.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pending, the README drift is scheduled for iteration 3.\\n- `playbook_capability`: notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `run-command-behaviour.mjs` imports `replayOffer` from `command-offer.mjs:56` and writes the\\n  live line through the local `appendRunLine` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:663-666`).\\n- `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1468-1478` reads `offeredAs` and splits a partner-side command\\n  out of the offer count. The two writers therefore feed one reader, and that reader is the\\n  only consumer of the new field in the changed area.\\n- The append gateway recorded the iteration record and the reducer reads its delta; both live\\n  under the lineage directory.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A line with no checkout or an untrusted checkout has no offer object with `offeredAs`; the\\n  `?? null` at `command-offer.mjs:496` keeps the field present with a null value. The reader\\n  treats a present command with a null side as an offer, which is the pre-fix behavior.\\n- A brief-only pass does not invent `offeredAs` for a legacy line. That is the documented\\n  contract at `command-offer.mjs:403-404`, and the reader's `offeredAs !== 'partner'` test\\n  keeps such a line counted as before.\\n- A head that names no command takes the `parseOffer` early return at `command-offer.mjs:73-75`,\\n  so `offeredAs` is null rather than a stale side.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `parseOffer` returns one of `head`, `partner` or null, and only the side of the first ` vs `\\n  before the match decides it (`command-offer.mjs:70-82`).\\n- Both writers preserve the field, and neither writes a partner-side command as an offer.\\n- The added backfill test asserts `partner` for the first line and null for the second\\n  (`command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`).\\n- The added helper test pins the field set and the null case\\n  (`command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:110-124`).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A missing `offeredAs` on the live writer: ruled out by `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203` and\\n  the helper return at `:820-827`.\\n- A missing `offeredAs` on the backfill writer: ruled out by `command-offer.mjs:496`.\\n- A partner-side command still counted as an offer: ruled out by\\n  `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`, which tests the side before counting.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: the Codex reader's resolved-path read, the holdout guard on the live capture path,\\n  and the runner's refusal to run holdout rows.\\n- Reason: the pass-four brief names both surfaces; iteration 1 covered the offer persistence.\\n- Rotation status: first security pass in this lineage.\\n- Required evidence: direct reads of `codex.mjs` containment and read, `identity.mjs`\\n  `resolveInside`, the Codex test tracker, and the runner's row guard.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680762882,"end":1794680778121}}}}
