{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681017946,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db531476002GSHV1Y2JCLgLw1","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db530838001zCofLagAxjgoH1","type":"tool","id":"call_ec9c951a8f8842f4bd657f84","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '40,100p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The attach module, scorer fusion, recommend handler and feature docs in the `scorer-attach`\n  area are the `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` lineage's scope. This lineage reads them only as\n  context evidence and raises no finding against them.\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n- No runtime command, build, test run or generator is executed; every claim is grounded in a\n  direct file read of the changed commit.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 3.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading both writers side by side against the one reader that consumes `offeredAs` closed the\n  P1 question without a test run: the field is present on every path that writes a line and the\n  reader is the only consumer. (iteration 1)\n- Tracing the brief-only branch separately caught the legacy-line behavior before it was mistaken\n  for a dropped field. (iteration 1)\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The attach module, scorer fusion, recommend handler and feature docs in the `scorer-attach`\n  area are the `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` lineage's scope. This lineage reads them only as\n  context evidence and raises no finding against them.\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n- No runtime command, build, test run or generator is executed; every claim is grounded in a\n  direct file read of the changed commit.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 3.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading both writers side by side against the one reader that consumes `offeredAs` closed the\n  P1 question without a test run: the field is present on every path that writes a line and the\n  reader is the only consumer. (iteration 1)\n- Tracing the brief-only branch separately caught the legacy-line behavior before it was mistaken\n  for a dropped field. (iteration 1)\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '40,100p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681017462,"end":1794681017946}}}}
