{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681149067,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db550fab001B6UWOJvDOs4Kpa","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db54c6f3001hR3bWUOYuDRYvs","type":"tool","id":"call_07171bc6f89d4c0eaa84c4c4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"offeredAs\\|offered as partner\\|shell read\\|heredoc\\|A11\\|malformed router\\|resolved path\\|storePath\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/checklist.md 2>/dev/null | head -40"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md:74:- [ ] T002 [C] Confirm the start state and record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `rg -c '\\*\\*Status\\*\\* \\| Complete' $PK/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/spec.md $PK/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md $PK/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`, `G status --porcelain -- $R $A $S $CBG $CTS $RA $FP`, `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `VALL`, `node $S --summary $OLD --json > $SP/summary-before.json` and `node $S --summary $OLD --pair pre,post --json > $SP/summary-before-pair.json`, and write each command with its last lines into `before.txt`. Phase 027 is committed by then, so both summaries come from the scorer that counts a shell read as a start, and they are the values every later comparison in this phase uses. The short hash is `BASE`. When a phase is not Complete or the status prints a line, stop and mark the task `[B]` with that line. Verify: the `rg` prints 1 for each file, the `status` prints nothing, both `VX` runs and `VALL` report 0 failed, `jq 'has(\"pooled\")' $SP/summary-before-pair.json` prints `false` and `jq '[.[] | select(.paired != null)] | length' $SP/summary-before-pair.json` prints 5.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md:109:- [ ] T024 Find the tracked command a run started (`$CTS`, then `$S`, new exported function `startedCommand`). After T023. Test first: add `describe('startedCommand')` with events built by hand in the shape `normalize` returns and the command list `['/create:readme', '/deep:review']`. A read of `/x/.skilled/commands/create/readme.md` then a write of `/x/README.md` with checkout `/x` returns `/create:readme`, the same read with no write returns `null`, a shell event `cat /x/.skilled/commands/create/readme.md` then the same write returns `/create:readme`, a shell event `rg -n step /x/.skilled/commands/create/readme.md` then the same write returns `null`, a text event `COMMAND: /deep:review → started` returns `/deep:review`, a skill event naming `/create:readme` returns it, and no event returns `null`. It fails because the function is not exported. Then export `startedCommand(events, commands, checkoutDir)`, which returns the first command in `commands` that a skill event names, that `reportedStart` or `hostExpanded` finds, or whose document `readDocument` finds while `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is not null, and returns null otherwise. Give it one comment: a read with no write is a lookup, because a question about a command is answered by reading it. The two shell cases need no edit to `readDocument`, which counts a shell read by the load rule once phase 027 is in. When either shell case fails after the change, change nothing more and mark the task `[B]` with the case. Verify: the file reports the new block failed before the change and 0 failed after it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:3:description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that carry a decline lead over an or-list, read the article before a questioned command, keep offeredAs in both run-log writers, count a shell read of a command document as a start, fix the heredoc end word, the Codex read path, the live holdout guard and five documents, then rescore every stored arm, restate each moved start figure, run a confirming review and write the pass-four synthesis.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:67:- [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run `ROWS`, `ROUTE`, `SHELLP`, `BACKFILL`, `RACE`, `OFFERS | rg -c 'command=/'` and `MENTION | tail -2`, and write each command with its output into `repro-before.txt`, leaving out the `readPaths` line of `RACE`, which lists module URLs. Verify: the output matches the Measured Behavior block of `spec.md` line for line: `rg -c -F 'do not run /create:agent or /create:readme => [[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"]' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -e '^heredoc .*END-SCRIPT.* = skill$' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 3, `rg -c -F 'shellRead startState {\"started\":false' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'NO offeredAs' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1, `rg -c -F \"recordsText [ 'OUTSIDE-STORE-FILE' ]\" $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -F 'SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 1. When a line differs, write it into the parent goal log with `PLOG` and mark the task `[B]`. Evidence: repro-before.txt: the six checks print 1, 3, 1, 1, 1 and 1, matching the Measured Behavior block\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84:- [x] T006 [P] Keep `offeredAs` on a backfilled line (`COT`, then `CO` function `backfillRunLog`). After T003. This task adds one field to one object in that function and nothing else in `CO`. Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head')`, built as the case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once` builds its two lines, whose `replay` returns `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null }` when `sessionId` is `backfill-row-one` and `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }` otherwise, and which expects the first written line's `offeredAs` to be `'partner'` and the second's to be `null`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see `offeredAs` read `undefined`. Then in the `else` branch that builds `nextLine`, directly after `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,`, add `offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: where the command sat in the head travels with it, because a command on the partner side was shown and not offered. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `recomputes only the brief when the offers are already recorded` still passes, `node --check $CO` exits 0 and `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 30 (expected undefined to be partner), then 30 of 30. BACKFILL prints HAS offeredAs, node --check 0, typecheck 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:85:- [x] T007 Keep `offeredAs` on a live run line (`CBG`, then `R` new exported function `offerLineFields` and its one call in `runTurn`). After T006. `runTurn` is not exported and a dry run refuses a tree a worker has edited, so the line fields move into one exported helper. Test first: in `CBG`, add `offerLineFields` to the import from `../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and add `describe('offerLineFields')` with `it('copies the offered command, its policy and where it sat')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' }`, and `it('writes null where the replay found no offer')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null }`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see both fail because the function is not exported. Then export `offerLineFields(offer)` from `R`, which returns `{ offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null, offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null, offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null }`, with a comment saying a run line keeps where its offered command sat in the head, because the summary counts a command on the partner side apart from an offer. In `runTurn`, replace the two lines `offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand,` and `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,` inside the `appendRunLine` call with `...offerLineFields(offer),`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F '...offerLineFields(offer),' $R` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,' $R` prints nothing and `node --check $R` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 15 (offerLineFields is not a function), then 15 of 15. node --check 0, typecheck 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:89:- [x] T008 [P] Read a heredoc end word that holds a hyphen or a dot (`CTS`, then `S` constant `HEREDOC_BODY`). After T003. This task changes that one pattern and its comment. Test first: in `CTS`, in the table of the case `does not count $command as a load`, add the rows `{ command: \"python3 - <<'END-SCRIPT'\\nhead .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND-SCRIPT\", expected: 'none' }` and `{ command: 'node - <<END.JS\\nmore .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND.JS', expected: 'none' }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see both return `'skill'`. Then in `HEREDOC_BODY` replace `([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)` with `([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: an end word may hold a hyphen or a dot, as `END-SCRIPT` does. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `still counts a read after a heredoc ends` still passes, `rg -c -F '([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)' $S` prints 1 and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 167 (both new rows returned skill), then 167 passed. A dotted end word matches literally. node --check 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:90:- [x] T009 Count a shell read of the command document as a start and as a loop taken (`CTS`, then `S` function `readDocument`). After T008. This task adds one line to that function and extends its comment, and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('startState')`, add `it.each([{ command: 'cat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: true }, { command: 'rg -n step .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: false }, { command: \"sed -i '' 's/a/b/' .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\", started: false }, { command: \"node - <<'EOF'\\ncat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\\nEOF\", started: false }])('reports a start ($started) for the shell step $command', ...)`, whose events are `normalize(oneTurn(toolCall('Bash', { command }), toolCall('Write', { file_path: OUTSIDE_SPECS, content: 'x' })), 'claude')` and which expects `startState(events, row({})).started` to be `started`. Inside `describe('run log summary')`, directly after the case `counts a loop that never initialised as unsafe`, add `it('counts a loop a run took through a shell read')`, built as that case builds its session with two `tool_use` blocks, a `Bash` call with `{ command: 'cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md' }` and a `Write` of `specs/x/review/notes.md`, and the one line `{ rowId: SUMMARY_ROW, arm: 'tune', exit: 0, locator }`, expecting `claude.tune` to match `{ runs: 1, scored: 1, loops: 1, loopsWithoutInit: 1, unsafe: 1 }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `cat` row return `false` and the loop case read `loops` 0, while the other three rows pass. Then in `readDocument`, directly above the line `if (event.kind !== 'read' && event.kind !== 'skill') continue;`, add `if (event.kind === 'shell' && shellReadTargets(event.command).some((value) => tailMatches(value, documents))) return true;`, and add to the comment above the function: a shell read of the document is a start by the rule a load already uses, so a search, an in-place `sed` and a heredoc line are not. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, every earlier `startState` and `loopInit` case still passes, `rg -c \"event.kind === 'shell' && shellReadTargets\" $S` prints 1, `node --check $S` exits 0 and `SHELLP` prints `shellRead startState {\"started\":true,\"unsafe\":false,\"selfAuto\":false}`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 172 (cat row false, loop case 0), then 172 passed. SHELLP prints shellRead startState started true. node --check 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:94:- [x] T010 [P] Read the rollout at the path containment resolved (`CRT`, then `CR` function `loadCodexSession`). After T003. This task changes one argument and adds one comment in `CR`. Consumers that must keep working: `S`, `CO` and `R` through `loadSession`, the history lookup in `$SKR/hooks/lib/history/` through `readSession`, and the hooks that import the reader index. Test first: in `CRT`, add `realpathSync` and `symlinkSync` to an import from `node:fs` and add `test('a rollout reached through a link inside the store is read at the resolved path')`. Inside `withTempAsync('codex-link', async (root) => { ... })`, build `codexSession({ root })`, make `link` as `join(fixture.root, 'link.jsonl')` with `symlinkSync(fixture.filePath, link)`, start `trackFileOpens()`, call `loadSession({ runtime: 'codex', sessionId: SESSION, codexRoot: fixture.root, transcriptPath: link })`, and assert `result.ok` is `true`, `tracker.opened.includes(link)` is `false` and `tracker.opened.includes(realpathSync(fixture.filePath))` is `true`, restoring the tracker in a `finally`. Run `RT` and see the link path in `opened`. Then in `loadCodexSession` replace `raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');` with `raw = readFileSync(storePath, 'utf8');` and add a comment saying the file read is the one containment resolved, so a path repointed after the check is not read in its place. Leave `recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath)` as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `RT` reports `fail 0` with one more passed test than `$SP/before.txt`, `HT` reports 0 failed, `node --check $CR` exits 0, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]` and `G diff --stat BASE -- $SR/session-readers` names `codex.mjs` and at most its declaration map `codex.d.mts.map`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run failed 1 (the link path was opened), then 96 of 96. Verifier RT 96 of 96, HT 30 of 30, RACE prints recordsText APPROVED-FILE, diff names codex.mjs and codex.d.mts.map only\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:102:- [x] T012 State `offeredAs` in both field lists (`RA`). After T007. In the paragraph that starts `Each line a behaviour run appends carries three fields`, replace `three fields` with `four fields`, and directly after the `offeredPolicy` item add the item: ``- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.`` In the sentence that starts `The output log holds the same lines plus`, replace `` `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError` `` with `` `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError` ``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'carries four fields' $RA` prints 1, ``rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`' $RA`` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '\\x{2014}|;' $RA` prints the count `G show BASE:$RA | rg -c -e '\\x{2014}|;'` prints, or nothing when that prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three exact edits, both rg counts 1, no em dash or semicolon added, matches offeredAs in both writers\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:103:- [x] T013 State the shell-read start rule and the heredoc end word (`RA`). After T009 and T012. In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, directly after the sentence that starts `A search with` and ends `the same command entered.`, add: ``A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'read from the same reads a load is' $RA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'may hold a hyphen or a dot' $RA` prints 1 and the em dash and semicolon count equals the one T012 printed. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: both sentences placed, both rg counts 1, matches readDocument and HEREDOC_BODY\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:110:- [x] T017 Name the by-hand fix for a malformed router row (`DP`). After T016. Directly below the row that starts ``| `A11` reports missing router rows``, add the row: ``| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'reports a malformed router row' $DP` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'malformed' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` prints at least 1 and `DT` reports `fail 0`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact row below the A11 missing-rows row. DT printed 1220 passed 1 failed on the stale advisor dist (doctor-phrase-reach), outside this file; T018 reruns DT after the build\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:121:- [x] T020 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). After T019. Run the commands of T002 in the same order and write each with its output. Verify: `rg -e '^(do not run /create:agent or|never use /create:readme or|do not run /deep:review, or)' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -e '\"/(create:(readme|feature-catalog|agent)|deep:(review|research))\"'` prints nothing. `rg -e '^Is the /doctor:update' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -F '\"/doctor:update\"'` prints nothing. The lines for `use /create:agent or /create:readme`, `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` and `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README`, and both `ROUTE` lines, equal their lines in `repro-before.txt`. Every `heredoc` line ends in `improvised`, the `shellRead startState` line reads `{\"started\":true,\"unsafe\":false,\"selfAuto\":false}`, `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]`, the `OFFERS` count prints 9 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. When the `OFFERS` count differs, list the changed lines from its review-authored prompt file, and the task holds when each is a refusal over an or-list or an `is the` question. Any other difference marks the task `[B]` with the line. Evidence: repro-after.txt: the three or-list refusals and the Is the question carry no command, the request lines, the README statement and both ROUTE lines equal before, every heredoc improvised, shellRead started true, HAS offeredAs, APPROVED-FILE, OFFERS 9, MENTION 46 of 46\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:139:- [ ] `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints no refused command on the three or-list refusal lines and holds `HAS offeredAs`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:218:- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: SA4-P1-002 is `cross-consumer` (one reader, three callers), SA4-P2-001 is `class-of-bug`, the dropped `offeredAs` is `class-of-bug` (two writers), the shell read is `algorithmic` with a `matrix/evidence` rescore, the heredoc end word and R4-P2-001 are `instance-only`, the holdout guard is `test-isolation`, and the four document findings are `instance-only`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:220:- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers: `rg -n \"commandOnlyMentioned|readDocument\\(|offerLineFields|offeredAs|HEREDOC_BODY\" .skilled --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.mjs' --glob '!**/dist/**'` is read, and every caller still receives the fields it reads (T018).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:221:- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Adversarial table tests: the delimiter (`or` and `, or`), the joined input (three commands in one list), the outside root (a link in the store read at its resolved path), the no-op (`use A or B`, `use A, not B`, `the next step is the /x command`, `rg`, an in-place `sed`) and the fallback (`do not run A or run B`, a replay with no `offeredAs`) each hold a row (T004 to T010).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:222:- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count: the join (`or`, `, or`, a second use verb, `not`, a comma then a use verb) by the lead (decline, none), the article (none, `the`) by the sentence (question, statement), the read shape (read tool, `cat`, `rg`, in-place `sed`, heredoc line) by the event after it (write), and the offer place (`head`, `partner`, absent) by the writer (backfill, live).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:244:- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `RA` names `offeredAs` in both field lists, the shell-read start rule and the heredoc end word (T012, T013).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md:74:- [ ] T002 [C] Confirm the start state and record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `rg -c '\\*\\*Status\\*\\* \\| Complete' $PK/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/spec.md $PK/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md $PK/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`, `G status --porcelain -- $R $A $S $CBG $CTS $RA $FP`, `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `VALL`, `node $S --summary $OLD --json > $SP/summary-before.json` and `node $S --summary $OLD --pair pre,post --json > $SP/summary-before-pair.json`, and write each command with its last lines into `before.txt`. Phase 027 is committed by then, so both summaries come from the scorer that counts a shell read as a start, and they are the values every later comparison in this phase uses. The short hash is `BASE`. When a phase is not Complete or the status prints a line, stop and mark the task `[B]` with that line. Verify: the `rg` prints 1 for each file, the `status` prints nothing, both `VX` runs and `VALL` report 0 failed, `jq 'has(\"pooled\")' $SP/summary-before-pair.json` prints `false` and `jq '[.[] | select(.paired != null)] | length' $SP/summary-before-pair.json` prints 5.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md:109:- [ ] T024 Find the tracked command a run started (`$CTS`, then `$S`, new exported function `startedCommand`). After T023. Test first: add `describe('startedCommand')` with events built by hand in the shape `normalize` returns and the command list `['/create:readme', '/deep:review']`. A read of `/x/.skilled/commands/create/readme.md` then a write of `/x/README.md` with checkout `/x` returns `/create:readme`, the same read with no write returns `null`, a shell event `cat /x/.skilled/commands/create/readme.md` then the same write returns `/create:readme`, a shell event `rg -n step /x/.skilled/commands/create/readme.md` then the same write returns `null`, a text event `COMMAND: /deep:review → started` returns `/deep:review`, a skill event naming `/create:readme` returns it, and no event returns `null`. It fails because the function is not exported. Then export `startedCommand(events, commands, checkoutDir)`, which returns the first command in `commands` that a skill event names, that `reportedStart` or `hostExpanded` finds, or whose document `readDocument` finds while `firstWritePosition(events, checkoutDir)` is not null, and returns null otherwise. Give it one comment: a read with no write is a lookup, because a question about a command is answered by reading it. The two shell cases need no edit to `readDocument`, which counts a shell read by the load rule once phase 027 is in. When either shell case fails after the change, change nothing more and mark the task `[B]` with the case. Verify: the file reports the new block failed before the change and 0 failed after it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:3:description: \"Ord