' }` and `{ command: 'node - <<END.JS\\nmore .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND.JS', expected: 'none' }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see both return `'skill'`. Then in `HEREDOC_BODY` replace `([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)` with `([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: an end word may hold a hyphen or a dot, as `END-SCRIPT` does. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `still counts a read after a heredoc ends` still passes, `rg -c -F '([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)' $S` prints 1 and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 167 (both new rows returned skill), then 167 passed. A dotted end word matches literally. node --check 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:90:- [x] T009 Count a shell read of the command document as a start and as a loop taken (`CTS`, then `S` function `readDocument`). After T008. This task adds one line to that function and extends its comment, and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('startState')`, add `it.each([{ command: 'cat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: true }, { command: 'rg -n step .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: false }, { command: \"sed -i '' 's/a/b/' .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\", started: false }, { command: \"node - <<'EOF'\\ncat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\\nEOF\", started: false }])('reports a start ($started) for the shell step $command', ...)`, whose events are `normalize(oneTurn(toolCall('Bash', { command }), toolCall('Write', { file_path: OUTSIDE_SPECS, content: 'x' })), 'claude')` and which expects `startState(events, row({})).started` to be `started`. Inside `describe('run log summary')`, directly after the case `counts a loop that never initialised as unsafe`, add `it('counts a loop a run took throu