n `CRT`, add `realpathSync` and `symlinkSync` to an import from `node:fs` and add `test('a rollout reached through a link inside the store is read at the resolved path')`. Inside `withTempAsync('codex-link', async (root) => { ... })`, build `codexSession({ root })`, make `link` as `join(fixture.root, 'link.jsonl')` with `symlinkSync(fixture.filePath, link)`, start `trackFileOpens()`, call `loadSession({ runtime: 'codex', sessionId: SESSION, codexRoot: fixture.root, transcriptPath: link })`, and assert `result.ok` is `true`, `tracker.opened.includes(link)` is `false` and `tracker.opened.includes(realpathSync(fixture.filePath))` is `true`, restoring the tracker in a `finally`. Run `RT` and see the link path in `opened`. Then in `loadCodexSession` replace `raw = readFileSync(transcriptPath, 'utf8');` with `raw = readFileSync(storePath, 'utf8');` and add a comment saying the file read is the one containment resolved, so a path repointed after the check is not read in its place. Leave `recordedSessionId(lines, transcriptPath)` as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `RT` reports `fail 0` with one more passed test than `$SP/before.txt`, `HT` reports 0 failed, `node --check $CR` exits 0, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]` and `G diff --stat BASE -- $SR/session-readers` names `codex.mjs` and at most its declaration map `codex.d.mts.map`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run failed 1 (the link path was opened), then 96 of 96. Verifier RT 96 of 96, HT 30 of 30, RACE prints recordsText APPROVED-FILE, diff names codex.mjs and codex.d.mts.map only\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:102:- [x] T012 State `offeredAs` in both field lists (`RA`). After T007. In the paragraph that starts `Each line a behaviour run appends carries three fields`, replace `three fields` with `four fields`, and directly after the `offeredPolicy` item add the item: ``- `offeredAs` says