embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'reports a malformed router row' $DP` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'malformed' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` prints at least 1 and `DT` reports `fail 0`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact row below the A11 missing-rows row. DT printed 1220 passed 1 failed on the stale advisor dist (doctor-phrase-reach), outside this file; T018 reruns DT after the build\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:121:- [x] T020 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). After T019. Run the commands of T002 in the same order and write each with its output. Verify: `rg -e '^(do not run /create:agent or|never use /create:readme or|do not run /deep:review, or)' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -e '\"/(create:(readme|feature-catalog|agent)|deep:(review|research))\"'` prints nothing. `rg -e '^Is the /doctor:update' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -F '\"/doctor:update\"'` prints nothing. The lines for `use /create:agent or /create:readme`, `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` and `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README`, and both `ROUTE` lines, equal their lines in `repro-before.txt`. Every `heredoc` line ends in `improvised`, the `shellRead startState` line reads `{\"started\":true,\"unsafe\":false,\"selfAuto\":false}`, `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]`, the `OFFERS` count prints 9 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. When the `OFFERS` count differs, list the changed lines from its review-authored prompt file, and the task holds when each is a refusal over an or-list or an `is the` question. Any other difference marks the task `[B]` with the line. Evidence: repro-after.txt: the three or-list refusals and the Is the question carry no command, the request lines, the README statement and both ROUTE lines equal before, every heredoc improvised, shellRead started true, HAS offeredAs, APPROVED-FILE, OFFERS 9, MENTION 46 of 46\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:139:- [ ] `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints no refused command on the three or-list refusal lines and holds `HAS offeredAs`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:218:- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: SA4-P1-002 is `cross-consumer` (one reader, three callers), SA4-P2-001 is `class-of-bug`, the dropped `offeredAs` is `class-of-bug` (two writers), the shell read is `algorithmic` with a `matrix/evidence` rescore, the heredoc end word and R4-P2-001 are `instance-only`, the holdout guard is `test-isolation`, and the four document findings are `instance-only`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:220:- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers: `rg -n \"commandOnlyMentioned|readDocument\\(|offerLineFields|offeredAs|HEREDOC_BODY\" .skilled --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.mjs' --glob '!**/dist/**'` is read, and every caller still receives the fields it reads (T018).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:221:- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Adversarial table tests: the delimiter (`or` and `, or`), the joined input (three commands in one list), the outside root (a link in the store read at its resolved path), the no-op (`use A or B`, `use A, not B`, `the next step is the /x command`, `rg`, an in-place `sed`) and the fallback (`do not run A or run B`, a replay with no `offeredAs`) each hold a row (T004 to T010).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:222:- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count: the join (`or`, `, or`, a second use verb, `not`, a comma then a use verb) by the lead (decline, none), the article (none, `the`) by the sentence (question, statement), the read shape (read tool, `cat`, `rg`, in-place `sed`, heredoc line) by the event after it (write), and the offer place (`head`, `partner`, absent) by the writer (backfill, live).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:244:- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `RA` names `offeredAs` in both field lists, the shell-read start rule and the heredoc end word (T012, T013).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"offeredAs\\\\|offered as partner\\\\|shell read\\\\|heredoc\\\\|A11\\\\|malformed router\\\\|resolved path\\\\|storePath\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/tasks.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/checklist.md 2>/dev/null | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681147307,"end":1794681149067}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681149093,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db55147b001vq6zwWR4HzLCRP","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db54c6f3001hR3bWUOYuDRYvs","type":"tool","id":"call_f552cd831dc04c7da084a997","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"offeredAs\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/ --include=*.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/implementation-summary.md:52:The packet's question is whether a model takes a real workflow more often, so the measure has to see a workflow load in every shape a runtime uses. A load is now a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the document (`cat`, `sed -n`, `head` and the other readers, not an in-place `sed`) or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror. A write outside the run's checkout, such as a temp note, no longer sets the boundary a load has to come before. A load of another mode under the owning hub is `otherMode`, apart from the skill's own load. An ask row whose run offered the command and waited is `asked`, and `askedActed` counts the asked runs that worked the task first. `followedRate` is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` keeps its rule and now shares that denominator, the six path counts, so no owned run leaves it. On the offer side, `parseOffer` says whether the command sat on the head or on its partner (`offeredAs`), and a head quoted inside a tool result no longer counts as a delivered brief.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/implementation-summary.md:62:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` | Modified | `offeredAs`, the tool-result rule and the replay note in the header |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/implementation-summary.md:116:| Reproductions | PASS, `skill,command,command,command,otherMode,skill,asked`, `offeredAs` `partner` once, no missed shell load or prompt mirror left |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/acceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given a head whose command sits after ` vs ` and a session whose only head is inside a tool result, When `parseOffer` and `briefDelivered` run, Then they return `offeredAs` `partner` and `false` | `npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. Observed at tasks.md:99 and tasks.md:100: command-offer tests 29 passed, 0 failed | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:99:- [x] T011 [P] Say whether the offered command sat on the head or on its partner (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('parseOffer')`, add `it('marks a command that sits after vs as the partner')` expecting `parseOffer('Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-code 0.95/0.12 vs sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.82/0.12 pass.')` to equal `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' }`, `it('marks a command before vs as the head')` expecting `offeredAs` `'head'` for `Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-doc → /create:agent (start) 0.82/0.12 vs sk-code 0.82/0.12 pass.`, a plain head expecting `'head'` and a head with no command expecting `offeredAs` `null`. Update the existing `toEqual` expectations in that describe to carry `offeredAs`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the new field missing. Then in `CO`'s `parseOffer`, return `offeredAs`: `null` with no match, `'partner'` when the text before the match holds ` vs `, and `'head'` otherwise, and name the field in the jsdoc with the reason that an ambiguous head names two paths and only one of them leads. Add `offeredAs: null` to `failedOffer`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` report 0 failed. Evidence: worker log first run Tests 6 failed, 21 passed (27), missing offeredAs. Passing run Tests 27 passed (27), guards 13 passed. Opus check PASS.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:104:- [x] T014 Describe the new fields, the load shapes and the delivery rule (`RA`). After lanes S and O. In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, after the sentence that lists the `workflow` fields phase 019 added, add: ``The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each.`` In the `command-offer.mjs` row, add: ``Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it.`` Verify: `rg -c \"askedActed\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"the Claude hook's replay\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"followedRate\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"offeredAs\" $RA` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"not each step followed\" $RA` prints 1. Evidence: doc task, checked by the coordinator. The diff adds the two sentences of the line verbatim to the two README rows and nothing else. rg counts askedActed 1, the Claude hook's replay 1, followedRate 1, offeredAs 1, not each step followed 1. No em dash or semicolon in added text.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:115:- [x] T017 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run both probes as T002 did. Verify: `sed -n '1,7p' $SP/repro-after.txt | cut -d: -f2 | tr -d ' ' | paste -sd, -` prints `skill,command,command,command,otherMode,skill,asked`, `rg -c -F '\"offeredAs\":\"partner\"' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 1 and `rg -c -e 'missed(ShellLoad|PromptMirror)=' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints at most the count in `$SP/repro-before.txt`, with each remaining one explained in `workflow-delta.txt` as a document that is not the row's own. Evidence: scratch/repro-after.txt: the seven path lines read skill,command,command,command,otherMode,skill,asked, offeredAs partner printed once, missedShellLoad and missedPromptMirror count 0 against 3 lines in repro-before.txt.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:206:- [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers: `rg -n \"workflowPath|firstWritePosition|parseOffer|offeredAs\" .skilled --glob '*.mjs' --glob '*.ts' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists every caller, and each still receives the fields it reads. Evidence: the rg lists S, CO and their two test files as the only callers in the advisor. The other three hits are unrelated local names in deep-loop and spec-kit tests.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:228:- [x] CHK-040 [P1] `RA` names `asked`, `askedActed`, `otherMode`, `followedRate` and `offeredAs` (T014). Evidence: the routing-accuracy README names asked, askedActed, otherMode, followedRate and offeredAs (T014).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/scratch/verify/022-workflow-measure-soundness-T011.md:6:- command-offer.mjs: failedOffer gains `offeredAs: null`. parseOffer returns `offeredAs: null` on no match, `'partner'` when `text.slice(0, match.index).includes(' vs ')`, else `'head'`. Jsdoc names the field with the reason (an ambiguous head names two paths and only one of them leads). replayOffer @returns updated to carry the field. Nothing else.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/scratch/verify/022-workflow-measure-soundness-T011.md:7:- command-offer.vitest.ts: the three existing parseOffer toEqual cases carry offeredAs ('head' for OFFERED_HEAD as the plain head, 'head' for AMBIGUOUS_HEAD whose command sits before vs, null for NO_COMMAND_HEAD as the head with no command). Two new cases with the exact names and inputs from the task line. The replayOffer hook_missing toEqual also gains `offeredAs: null`, which is the forced consequence of the failedOffer change the task asks for, not an extra behaviour.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/scratch/verify/022-workflow-measure-soundness-T011.md:11:- Worker log first run: `Tests  6 failed | 21 passed (27)`, failing cases: the five parseOffer cases and replayOffer \"reports a checkout without the prompt hook instead of throwing\", all for the missing offeredAs field.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/scratch/verify/022-workflow-measure-soundness-T011.md:19:The partner test checks only text before the first command match, so a command in the head clause of an ambiguous head stays 'head' even though ` vs ` follows it (covered by AMBIGUOUS_HEAD and the new /create:agent case). A plain head has no ` vs `. No realistic misclassification found. Note, not a defect: the two literal offer objects in the run loop (no_checkout, untrusted_checkout) and the written line fields do not carry offeredAs. The task did not ask for that, and later tasks or T014 may.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/plan.md:65:- **`offeredAs` in the offer module**: without it an offer on the partner side reads as the head's offer. No new file, option or dependency.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/plan.md:85:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Spreads the replayed offer onto a run line | a consumer: a new line gains `offeredAs`. Unchanged | `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/plan.md:86:| Stored run logs | Hold `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` with no `offeredAs` | unchanged. The summary reads the two old fields only | Both summary runs exit 0 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/plan.md:92:- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n \"workflowPath|firstWritePosition|followedBeforeWrite|parseOffer|offeredAs\" .skilled --glob '*.mjs' --glob '*.ts' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/spec.md:110:| A-11, the partner's command | `parseOffer` takes the first slash command on the line | It reports `offeredAs` as `head` or `partner` (T011) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/spec.md:143:| `RAD/command-offer.mjs` | Modify | `offeredAs`, the tool-result rule and the module header |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/spec.md:172:| REQ-008 | `parseOffer` returns `offeredAs` `partner` for a command that sits after ` vs ` and `head` otherwise, and `briefDelivered` returns `false` when only a tool result holds a head. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/implementation-summary.md:52:The packet's question is whether a model takes a real workflow more often, so the measure has to see a workflow load in every shape a runtime uses. A load is now a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the document (`cat`, `sed -n`, `head` and the other readers, not an in-place `sed`) or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror. A write outside the run's checkout, such as a temp note, no longer sets the boundary a load has to come before. A load of another mode under the owning hub is `otherMode`, apart from the skill's own load. An ask row whose run offered the command and waited is `asked`, and `askedActed` counts the asked runs that worked the task first. `followedRate` is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` keeps its rule and now shares that denominator, the six path counts, so no owned run leaves it. On the offer side, `parseOffer` says whether the command sat on the head or on its partner (`offeredAs`), and a head quoted inside a tool result no longer counts as a delivered brief.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/implementation-summary.md:62:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` | Modified | `offeredAs`, the tool-result rule and the replay note in the header |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/implementation-summary.md:116:| Reproductions | PASS, `skill,command,command,command,otherMode,skill,asked`, `offeredAs` `partner` once, no missed shell load or prompt mirror left |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/acceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given a head whose command sits after ` vs ` and a session whose only head is inside a tool result, When `parseOffer` and `briefDelivered` run, Then they return `offeredAs` `partner` and `false` | `npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. Observed at tasks.md:99 and tasks.md:100: command-offer tests 29 passed, 0 failed | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:99:- [x] T011 [P] Say whether the offered command sat on the head or on its partner (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('parseOffer')`, add `it('marks a command that sits after vs as the partner')` expecting `parseOffer('Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-code 0.95/0.12 vs sk-doc → /create:manual-testing-playbook (start) 0.82/0.12 pass.')` to equal `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' }`, `it('marks a command before vs as the head')` expecting `offeredAs` `'head'` for `Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-doc → /create:agent (start) 0.82/0.12 vs sk-code 0.82/0.12 pass.`, a plain head expecting `'head'` and a head with no command expecting `offeredAs` `null`. Update the existing `toEqual` expectations in that describe to carry `offeredAs`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the new field missing. Then in `CO`'s `parseOffer`, return `offeredAs`: `null` with no match, `'partner'` when the text before the match holds ` vs `, and `'head'` otherwise, and name the field in the jsdoc with the reason that an ambiguous head names two paths and only one of them leads. Add `offeredAs: null` to `failedOffer`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` report 0 failed. Evidence: worker log first run Tests 6 failed, 21 passed (27), missing offeredAs. Passing run Tests 27 passed (27), guards 13 passed. Opus check PASS.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:104:- [x] T014 Describe the new fields, the load shapes and the delivery rule (`RA`). After lanes S and O. In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, after the sentence that lists the `workflow` fields phase 019 added, add: ``The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each.`` In the `command-offer.mjs` row, add: ``Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it.`` Verify: `rg -c \"askedActed\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"the Claude hook's replay\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"followedRate\" $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c \"offeredAs\" $RA` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"not each step followed\" $RA` prints 1. Evidence: doc task, checked by the coordinator. The diff adds the two sentences