{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681170283,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db55670400186aktPqygqvsrF","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db551c9e001XgpzbJm01NjQWY","type":"tool","id":"call_6a72a08cdbe84fb2af5d74c6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"P2 Findings\" -A 25 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-004.md | head -40"},"output":"31:### P2 Findings\n32-\n33-1. **The changed test tables leave all four residual behaviors unpinned** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39` -- The `REFUSE8` table holds eight single-command refusals or requests and no coordinated refusal; the small-edit table holds the two exact `REQ-004` controls and the creation controls, but no correction with a generic creation word; `QUESTION2` holds two questions but not the `Is the X command` noun form. The changed tests are therefore green while the four behaviors from iterations 1 to 3 are live. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39]\n34-   Finding class: test_coverage_gap\n35-   Scope proof: the test file is in the declared scope; each missing input is a prompt the changed functions already accept, and the current helper probes return the wrong result for it.\n36-   Affected surface hints: `REFUSE8`, the small-edit `it.each`, `QUESTION2`, the phase 020 `CHK-FIX-004` evidence.\n37-   Case: adding `['do not run /deep:review or /deep:research', '/deep:research']` to `REFUSE8` fails today because `commandOnlyMentioned` returns false; adding `fix the typo in the readme and make sure the grammar is right` to the small-edit `offers no creation command` cases fails because `attachCommand` returns `/create:readme`; adding `['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update']` to `QUESTION2` fails because the bare-ask lead does not allow the noun `command`. The packet's `CHK-FIX-004` claims a \"two commands\" adversarial case, but the table's two-command case is the request `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` (`:181`), not a coordinated refusal.\n38-\n39-## Traceability Checks\n40-\n41-- `spec_code` -- partial (unchanged from iteration 3): the one active P1 is the coordinated refusal; the two accepted limits are recorded as P2s; the REQ-007 text is stale.\n42-- `checklist_evidence` -- partial: the phase checklist's `CHK-FIX-004` overstates the two-command coverage; `AC-007` records 9 against `REQ-007`'s 10.\n43-- `feature_catalog_code` -- partial (unchanged from iteration 3): the two stale docs are P2s.\n44-- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable.\n45-- `agent_cross_runtime` -- partial: no runtime branch; live proof belongs to the phase 007 arm.\n46-- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable.\n47-\n48-## Integration Evidence\n49-\n50-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-56` is the `REFUSE8` table; `:181` is the two-command request; `:135-432` is the small-edit suite; `:50-53` is `QUESTION2`.\n51-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414` is the every-occurrence rule the coordinated refusal misses; `:331` and `:487` are the creation-word guard; `:389` is the bare-ask lead.\n52-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209` is the gate the doctor question row survives.\n53-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:382-482` pins the two scorer gates themselves, but no case connects the mention reader to the `Is the X command` form.\n54-- The six changed test files still report 191 passed; the gap is missing inputs, not a failing assertion.\n55-\n56-## Edge Cases\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31:### P2 Findings\n32-\n33-1. **The changed test tables leave all four residual behaviors unpinned** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39` -- The `REFUSE8` table holds eight single-command refusals or requests and no coordinated refusal; the small-edit table holds the two exact `REQ-004` controls and the creation controls, but no correction with a generic creation word; `QUESTION2` holds two questions but not the `Is the X command` noun form. The changed tests are therefore green while the four behaviors from iterations 1 to 3 are live. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39]\n34-   Finding class: test_coverage_gap\n35-   Scope proof: the test file is in the declared scope; each missing input is a prompt the changed functions already accept, and the current helper probes return the wrong result for it.\n36-   Affected surface hints: `REFUSE8`, the small-edit `it.each`, `QUESTION2`, the phase 020 `CHK-FIX-004` evidence.\n37-   Case: adding `['do not run /deep:review or /deep:research', '/deep:research']` to `REFUSE8` fails today because `commandOnlyMentioned` returns false; adding `fix the typo in the readme and make sure the grammar is right` to the small-edit `offers no creation command` cases fails because `attachCommand` returns `/create:readme`; adding `['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update']` to `QUESTION2` fails because the bare-ask lead does not allow the noun `command`. The packet's `CHK-FIX-004` claims a \"two commands\" adversarial case, but the table's two-command case is the request `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` (`:181`), not a coordinated refusal.\n38-\n39-## Traceability Checks\n40-\n41-- `spec_code` -- partial (unchanged from iteration 3): the one active P1 is the coordinated refusal; the two accepted limits are recorded as P2s; the REQ-007 text is stale.\n42-- `checklist_evidence` -- partial: the phase checklist's `CHK-FIX-004` overstates the two-command coverage; `AC-007` records 9 against `REQ-007`'s 10.\n43-- `feature_catalog_code` -- partial (unchanged from iteration 3): the two stale docs are P2s.\n44-- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable.\n45-- `agent_cross_runtime` -- partial: no runtime branch; live proof belongs to the phase 007 arm.\n46-- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable.\n47-\n48-## Integration Evidence\n49-\n50-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-56` is the `REFUSE8` table; `:181` is the two-command request; `:135-432` is the small-edit suite; `:50-53` is `QUESTION2`.\n51-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414` is the every-occurrence rule the coordinated refusal misses; `:331` and `:487` are the creation-word guard; `:389` is the bare-ask lead.\n52-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209` is the gate the doctor question row survives.\n53-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:382-482` pins the two scorer gates themselves, but no case connects the mention reader to the `Is the X command` form.\n54-- The six changed test files still report 191 passed; the gap is missing inputs, not a failing assertion.\n55-\n56-## Edge Cases\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"P2 Findings\\\" -A 25 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-004.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681169668,"end":1794681170283}}}}
