{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681210672,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db55b0520017TNcYw2cxo3j74","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db55a2c5001TblreLp558Ch2K","type":"tool","id":"call_86618c9cb9104ef0b880c18a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 3\n\n- Mode: review\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`\n- Iteration: 3 of 3\n- Dimension: RECOVERY (least-covered traceability and maintainability)\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (8-10 read actions)\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4b.txt`, `steer.md` (absent), `review/verify-4/report.md`, phase 027 `tasks.md`, the iteration-2 narrative\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`. The recovery pass changes\ngranularity from code to line-level doc claims. It checks the two shared docs this area changed\n(`routing-accuracy/README.md` and `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`) against the code and the\ntask rows that claim them.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-80,120-126,183-188`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:255-272`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1170-1209`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84-110,218-244`\n\nContext reads: `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and\n`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410,782-803` for the A11 claim;\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:488-501`\nfor the backfill field set.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76` -- The backfill now writes `offeredAs` as a fourth attribution field (`command-offer.mjs:496`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:824`), and the output sentence at `:188` names it, but the paragraph at `:76` still says \"adds those three fields\" and the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row at `:125` still says `--backfill` rewrites with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered`. A reader following the section learns a three-field contract that the code no longer has. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76]\n   Finding class: doc_code_drift\n   Scope proof: the README is in the declared accuracy-runner scope; the two code lines are the changed writers, and phase 027 T012 claims the README field lists.\n   Affected surface hints: README backfill section, runner table row, the `offeredAs` attribution contract.\n   Case: run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill in.jsonl --out out.jsonl`; every output line carries `offeredAs` (pinned by `command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`), while `README.md:76` says three fields and `:125` names only three.\n\n2. **The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65` -- `runTurn` appends the head-moved line before the offer replay at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`, so that line has no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` or `briefDelivered`. The blanket sentence is false for the exit-3 path the README itself documents. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65]\n   Finding class: doc_code_drift\n   Scope proof: the README and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both in the declared scope; the early append is the same writer's own branch.\n   Affected surface hints: head-moved run line, exit 3, attribution contract, scorer's `offerFieldAbsent`.\n   Case: a turn that commits or stashes during the run sets `headMoved`; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183` appends `{ ...line, restored: false, headMoved: true }` and returns exit 3. The written JSON has none of the four fields, while `README.md:65` says each appended line carries them. A scorer reading that line sees `offerFieldAbsent` even though the run line is valid.\n\nThe A11 malformed-router row added at\n`doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:268` agrees with the code: the doctor check reports\n`malformed <kind> row at line N: C cells where the header has H`\n(`agents-md-check.cjs:776-778`), and the embed only splices missing rows into the table\n(`agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410`), so the advice to fix the row by hand matches what embed will\nand will not do. No finding.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 027 T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with\n  evidence, and the code matches T006/T007/T010. T012's \"both field lists\" is narrower than the\n  README's actual field lists: the backfill paragraph and the runner table row still say three\n  fields.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. `CHK-040` (tasks.md:244) asks `RA` to name `offeredAs` in both\n  field lists; the two lists T012 edited are correct, but the backfill lists are the remaining\n  drift. `CHK-FIX-003` and `CHK-FIX-004` remain open with the phase.\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the two changed\n  writers; the routing-accuracy README is the shared doc.\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers.\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed.\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The routing-accuracy README is the only shared doc that describes `command-offer.mjs` and\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs`; phase 027 T012 and T013 edit it as the doc of record.\n- The doctor presentation asset is the `/doctor:agents-md` troubleshooting text. Its new row\n  points at the same two scripts the doctor check and embed run:\n  `agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and `agents-md-embed.cjs:782-803`.\n- The head-moved branch is the same `runTurn` function that now spreads `offerLineFields`; the\n  early return at `:1180-1184` is the one path that never reaches the offer replay.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A malformed shipped router row makes the checker report it as malformed and as missing. The\n  embed then adds a second, well-formed copy of that shipped row, and the malformed row stays.\n  The added A11 advice does not warn about the duplicate; the row still says embed never rewrites\n  a row, which is true, and the operator is told to fix the row by hand. Recorded as an operator\n  note, not a finding, because the added text does not claim the duplicate cannot happen.\n- The backfill's `--brief-only` path leaves a legacy line without `offeredAs`, which the README's\n  `--brief-only` paragraph already covers. The stale \"three fields\" paragraph is about the\n  default path, so the two statements do not conflict.\n- A head-moved line is written before `restoreTurn`, so `leftoverPaths` is absent too. The\n  README's head-moved paragraph names only `restored` and the changed paths; this is consistent\n  with the line and part of the same all-or-nothing early return.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The A11 malformed-row guidance matches the checker's message and the embed's insert-only\n  behavior.\n- The top attribution list (`README.md:65-70`) now names four fields, including `offeredAs`.\n- The output sentence (`README.md:188`) names `offeredAs` alongside the other backfill fields.\n- Phase 027 task rows T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with evidence that\n  matches the changed lines this lineage read.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names\n  the cell count and the header width, and the embed only adds missing rows.\n- **The top attribution list still says three fields.** Ruled out: `README.md:65` says four and\n  the item at `:69` defines `offeredAs`.\n- **The output-log sentence still omits `offeredAs`.** Ruled out: `README.md:188` lists it.\n- **The backfill paragraph's \"three fields\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the\n  paragraph introduces the default backfill, and the separate `--brief-only` paragraph is the\n  one that describes copying offer fields untouched.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining within the cap; synthesis\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry, the three deltas and the\n  documentation findings.\n- Reason: three iterations are complete, two clean code dimensions and two P2 doc drifts; the\n  cap is reached without a legal convergence stop.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability and maintainability covered by\n  the recovery pass (partial, because the packet's checklist is still open).\n- Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the three iteration final lines and the\n  synthesis report.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach.\n- Recovery note: the recovery pass changed granularity to line-level doc claims and produced the\n  two findings.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo active P0 or P1 finding. Two P2 documentation drifts remain active; the verdict is PASS with\nadvisories.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 3\\n\\n- Mode: review\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`\\n- Run: `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`\\n- Iteration: 3 of 3\\n- Dimension: RECOVERY (least-covered traceability and maintainability)\\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (8-10 read actions)\\n- Sources read: `review-brief-4b.txt`, `steer.md` (absent), `review/verify-4/report.md`, phase 027 `tasks.md`, the iteration-2 narrative\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n`/deep:review` fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`. The recovery pass changes\\ngranularity from code to line-level doc claims. It checks the two shared docs this area changed\\n(`routing-accuracy/README.md` and `doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`) against the code and the\\ntask rows that claim them.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-80,120-126,183-188`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:255-272`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1170-1209`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:84-110,218-244`\\n\\nContext reads: `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and\\n`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410,782-803` for the A11 claim;\\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:488-501`\\nfor the backfill field set.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76` -- The backfill now writes `offeredAs` as a fourth attribution field (`command-offer.mjs:496`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:824`), and the output sentence at `:188` names it, but the paragraph at `:76` still says \\\"adds those three fields\\\" and the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row at `:125` still says `--backfill` rewrites with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered`. A reader following the section learns a three-field contract that the code no longer has. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76]\\n   Finding class: doc_code_drift\\n   Scope proof: the README is in the declared accuracy-runner scope; the two code lines are the changed writers, and phase 027 T012 claims the README field lists.\\n   Affected surface hints: README backfill section, runner table row, the `offeredAs` attribution contract.\\n   Case: run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill in.jsonl --out out.jsonl`; every output line carries `offeredAs` (pinned by `command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`), while `README.md:76` says three fields and `:125` names only three.\\n\\n2. **The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65` -- `runTurn` appends the head-moved line before the offer replay at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184`, so that line has no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` or `briefDelivered`. The blanket sentence is false for the exit-3 path the README itself documents. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65]\\n   Finding class: doc_code_drift\\n   Scope proof: the README and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both in the declared scope; the early append is the same writer's own branch.\\n   Affected surface hints: head-moved run line, exit 3, attribution contract, scorer's `offerFieldAbsent`.\\n   Case: a turn that commits or stashes during the run sets `headMoved`; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183` appends `{ ...line, restored: false, headMoved: true }` and returns exit 3. The written JSON has none of the four fields, while `README.md:65` says each appended line carries them. A scorer reading that line sees `offerFieldAbsent` even though the run line is valid.\\n\\nThe A11 malformed-router row added at\\n`doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt:268` agrees with the code: the doctor check reports\\n`malformed <kind> row at line N: C cells where the header has H`\\n(`agents-md-check.cjs:776-778`), and the embed only splices missing rows into the table\\n(`agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410`), so the advice to fix the row by hand matches what embed will\\nand will not do. No finding.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- partial. Phase 027 T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with\\n  evidence, and the code matches T006/T007/T010. T012's \\\"both field lists\\\" is narrower than the\\n  README's actual field lists: the backfill paragraph and the runner table row still say three\\n  fields.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. `CHK-040` (tasks.md:244) asks `RA` to name `offeredAs` in both\\n  field lists; the two lists T012 edited are correct, but the backfill lists are the remaining\\n  drift. `CHK-FIX-003` and `CHK-FIX-004` remain open with the phase.\\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the two changed\\n  writers; the routing-accuracy README is the shared doc.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- notApplicable. No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers.\\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable. No agent definition changed.\\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable. No playbook surface changed.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The routing-accuracy README is the only shared doc that describes `command-offer.mjs` and\\n  `run-command-behaviour.mjs`; phase 027 T012 and T013 edit it as the doc of record.\\n- The doctor presentation asset is the `/doctor:agents-md` troubleshooting text. Its new row\\n  points at the same two scripts the doctor check and embed run:\\n  `agents-md-check.cjs:757-808` and `agents-md-embed.cjs:782-803`.\\n- The head-moved branch is the same `runTurn` function that now spreads `offerLineFields`; the\\n  early return at `:1180-1184` is the one path that never reaches the offer replay.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A malformed shipped router row makes the checker report it as malformed and as missing. The\\n  embed then adds a second, well-formed copy of that shipped row, and the malformed row stays.\\n  The added A11 advice does not warn about the duplicate; the row still says embed never rewrites\\n  a row, which is true, and the operator is told to fix the row by hand. Recorded as an operator\\n  note, not a finding, because the added text does not claim the duplicate cannot happen.\\n- The backfill's `--brief-only` path leaves a legacy line without `offeredAs`, which the README's\\n  `--brief-only` paragraph already covers. The stale \\\"three fields\\\" paragraph is about the\\n  default path, so the two statements do not conflict.\\n- A head-moved line is written before `restoreTurn`, so `leftoverPaths` is absent too. The\\n  README's head-moved paragraph names only `restored` and the changed paths; this is consistent\\n  with the line and part of the same all-or-nothing early return.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The A11 malformed-row guidance matches the checker's message and the embed's insert-only\\n  behavior.\\n- The top attribution list (`README.md:65-70`) now names four fields, including `offeredAs`.\\n- The output sentence (`README.md:188`) names `offeredAs` alongside the other backfill fields.\\n- Phase 027 task rows T006, T007, T010, T012, T013 and T017 are marked `[x]` with evidence that\\n  matches the changed lines this lineage read.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The A11 row contradicts the doctor check.** Ruled out: the checker's malformed message names\\n  the cell count and the header width, and the embed only adds missing rows.\\n- **The top attribution list still says three fields.** Ruled out: `README.md:65` says four and\\n  the item at `:69` defines `offeredAs`.\\n- **The output-log sentence still omits `offeredAs`.** Ruled out: `README.md:188` lists it.\\n- **The backfill paragraph's \\\"three fields\\\" is correct for `--brief-only`.** Ruled out: the\\n  paragraph introduces the default backfill, and the separate `--brief-only` paragraph is the\\n  one that describes copying offer fields untouched.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining within the cap; synthesis\\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry, the three deltas and the\\n  documentation findings.\\n- Reason: three iterations are complete, two clean code dimensions and two P2 doc drifts; the\\n  cap is reached without a legal convergence stop.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete; traceability and maintainability covered by\\n  the recovery pass (partial, because the packet's checklist is still open).\\n- Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the three iteration final lines and the\\n  synthesis report.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach.\\n- Recovery note: the recovery pass changed granularity to line-level doc claims and produced the\\n  two findings.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nNo active P0 or P1 finding. Two P2 documentation drifts remain active; the verdict is PASS with\\nadvisories.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681188434,"end":1794681210672}}}}
