{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681396402,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","part":{"partID":"prt_1db584643001STUFshNd076A3n","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad86ffemxqRFlUJ7Tx0bg","messageID":"msg_1db5815ea001cAj9gYIwJC3nRt","type":"tool","id":"call_aa5549aa7a0e4a7299ee1ac1","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Four (accuracy-runner lineage)\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the confirming round of review pass four, on the fix range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`, area `accuracy-runner`, run `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`, executor `cli-opencode` `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max.\n- Reviewed scope: the nine paths in `review/review-scope-4b.txt` whose area is `accuracy-runner` — the routing-accuracy offer and runner pair, their two changed tests, the Codex session reader and its test, the Codex declaration map, and the doctor presentation row — plus the shared README that describes the pair.\n- Inputs to this synthesis: the three iteration narratives, the three delta files, the lineage registry (2 active P2 findings), the strategy and the dashboard.\n- Cross-area boundary: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the scorer modules, the feature docs and `score-command-transcripts.mjs` belong to `scorer-attach-confirm-4b`. This lineage read them only as context and raises no finding against them.\n- Iteration cap: 3 of 3. The loop stopped at the cap; convergence was not declared.\n- Operator review focus: Confirming round of review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and follow specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4b.txt: it names the scope file, the commit range, which files your lineage reviews and the checks. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Verdict: PASS.** No P0 and no P1 findings are active.\n- **hasAdvisories: true.** Two P2 documentation drifts remain active.\n- **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 0, P2 2.\n- **The P1 that this round confirms is fixed.** `offeredAs` now travels from `parseOffer` through both run-log writers: the backfill at `command-offer.mjs:496` and the live turn at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203` via `offerLineFields`. The scorer's single consumer reads the field at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\n- **The Codex containment P2 is fixed.** `resolveInside` realpaths both sides and the reader now opens `storePath` (`codex.mjs:169`). The new test proves the link path is never opened and the resolved file is (`codex.test.mjs:117-127`).\n- **The holdout guard holds in this area.** `findRow` refuses a split-holdout row before its prompt can reach a child (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:633-634`), and the G2 fixed prompts are runner-owned ids absent from both corpora. The live-capture half of the guard is present in the sibling area at `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:206-210`.\n- **The A11 malformed-row guidance agrees with the code.** The checker reports the cell count against the header width (`agents-md-check.cjs:776-778`), and the embed only splices missing rows (`agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410`).\n- **The two P2s are README drift, not code drift.** The backfill paragraph still says three fields (`README.md:76`) and the runner table row lists three (`README.md:125`); the blanket \"every line carries four fields\" sentence (`README.md:65`) is false for the head-moved line written at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183`.\n- **Holdout hygiene:** no prompt was opened or printed. Corpus work was limited to `jq 'del(.prompt)'` id and split counts and to source-level row lookup. Holdout prompt text was never read.\n- **Cross-runtime:** the changed Codex reader is shared; the runner's prompt and refusal logic is runtime-neutral. No live per-runtime session was captured in this lineage.\n- **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached; no convergence event was recorded, and the packet checklist is still open.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nNo plan is required for the PASS verdict. The two P2s are advisory documentation corrections that can fold into phase 027 T012's follow-up; they do not block release.\n\n```json Planning Packet\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"triggerReason\": \"PASS with two advisory documentation drifts; no P0 or P1 remains.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"counts\": { \"p0\": 0, \"p1\": 0, \"p2\": 2, \"active\": 2, \"iterations\": 3 },\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR4B-P2-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"doc_code_drift\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR4B-P2-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"doc_code_drift\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"advisory\": true,\n      \"name\": \"README attribution contract\",\n      \"files\": [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"],\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"Change the backfill paragraph at :76 from three fields to four and name offeredAs.\",\n        \"Add offeredAs to the run-command-behaviour field list at :125.\",\n        \"Qualify the every-line sentence at :65 for the head-moved line, or state the exception beside the head-moved paragraph.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"The routing-accuracy README is the doc of record for the two writers; its field lists must match the six fields the backfill writes and the four the live turn writes.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Edit README.md:76 and :125 to name offeredAs.\",\n    \"Edit README.md:65 to name the head-moved exception, or move the four-field statement under a completed-turn qualification.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"doc_code_drift\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"routing-accuracy README attribution section\",\n    \"run-command-behaviour head_moved path\",\n    \"command-offer backfill output contract\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### AR4B-P2-001 — The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row\n\n- Severity: P2\n- Dimension: traceability\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76`\n- Finding class: `doc_code_drift`\n- Evidence: `README.md:76` says \"adds those three fields\"; `README.md:125` says `--backfill` rewrites with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered`; `README.md:188` already names `offeredAs`; `command-offer.mjs:496` and `run-command-behaviour.mjs:824` write it.\n- Case: run `--backfill`; every output line carries `offeredAs` (pinned by `command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`), while the paragraph and the row count three.\n- Fix: change \"three\" to \"four\" in the backfill paragraph and add `offeredAs` to the runner table row's field list.\n- Scope proof: the README is in the declared scope; the two code lines are the changed writers.\n- Affected surface hints: README backfill section, runner table row, the `offeredAs` attribution contract.\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\n\n### AR4B-P2-002 — The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none\n\n- Severity: P2\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65`\n- Finding class: `doc_code_drift`\n- Evidence: `README.md:65` says each appended line carries four fields; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184` appends `{ ...line, restored: false, headMoved: true }` before the offer replay and returns exit 3.\n- Case: a turn that commits or stashes during the run sets `headMoved`; the written line has no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` or `briefDelivered`, and the scorer reads it as `offerFieldAbsent`.\n- Fix: qualify the sentence for a completed turn, or name the head-moved exception in the paragraph that already documents exit 3.\n- Scope proof: the README and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both in the declared scope.\n- Affected surface hints: head-moved run line, exit 3, attribution contract, scorer `offerFieldAbsent`.\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n### P0 — none\n\n### P1 — none\n\n### P2 — advisory documentation\n\n1. README attribution contract (`routing-accuracy/README.md`):\n   - `:76` — three → four, and name `offeredAs`.\n   - `:125` — add `offeredAs` to the `--backfill` field list.\n   - `:65` — qualify the every-line sentence for the head-moved line, or name the exception in the exit-3 paragraph.\n\nThese edits touch one file and no code. They can fold into the phase 027 T012 follow-up.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The README's attribution section owns four live-turn fields (`offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `briefDelivered`) and six backfill fields (the four plus `offerError` and `offerBackfilled`).\n- The head-moved line is a partial record by construction: it is written before the replay and the restore. Any \"every line\" statement must exclude it or say what it carries.\n- Phase 027 T012's \"both field lists\" reading should include the backfill paragraph and the runner table row, not only the top list and the output sentence.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Update `README.md:76` to four fields and name `offeredAs`.\n- Update `README.md:125` to add `offeredAs` to the backfill field list.\n- Update `README.md:65` and the head-moved paragraph so the partial line is explicit.\n- Re-run the README's own counts if any are asserted; no code or test change is needed.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Phase 027 T006/T007/T010/T012/T013/T017 are `[x]` with evidence and the code matches T006/T007/T010. T012's \"both field lists\" misses the backfill paragraph and runner row (AR4B-P2-001). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | `CHK-040` asks `RA` to name `offeredAs` in both field lists; the two lists T012 edited are correct, the backfill lists remain stale. `CHK-FIX-003`/`CHK-FIX-004` stay open with the phase. |\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers; the Codex reader is shared and tested directly. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog page describes the two changed writers. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\n\n### AC_COVERAGE\n\n`exempt`. The review target's root folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md`; the phase children hold\ntheir own criteria, and this lineage's scope is the changed `accuracy-runner` files.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Residual Codex read race.** A target replaced after `realpathSync` but before `readFileSync`\n  remains a narrow race. The verify report's probe (a link swapped before containment) is fixed;\n  closing the residual needs an `open` with a no-follow flag, which is outside this change.\n- **A11 duplicate-row note.** A malformed shipped router row is reported as malformed and as\n  missing, so an embed adds a second, well-formed copy and leaves the malformed row. The new A11\n  row does not claim otherwise; it is an operator note, not a finding.\n- **Sibling surfaces.** The live-capture holdout guard (`command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`), the\n  scorer's `paired` key and `unscoredOnly`, and the feature docs are the sibling lineage's\n  findings and are not re-reported here.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: none.\n- Failed pivots: none.\n- Audited overrides: none.\n- Swept directions: none; the three iterations covered correctness, security and the\n  traceability/maintainability recovery pass.\n- Selected review directions: offer persistence, Codex containment, holdout guard, README and\n  doctor row agreement.\n- Remaining frontier: the packet checklist is still open, so traceability and maintainability are\n  recorded as partial rather than complete.\n- This section records breadth only. It does not change the Executive Summary, the finding\n  registry or the verdict.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Search Ledger\n\n### Search Coverage\n\n- Required bug classes: `field_persistence`, `writer_parity`, `partner_semantics`,\n  `doc_code_drift`, `symlink_escape`, `resolved_path_toctou`, `holdout_leak`,\n  `untrusted_checkout_execution`, `checklist_evidence`.\n- Covered: `doc_code_drift`, `checklist_evidence`.\n- Ruled out: `field_persistence`, `writer_parity`, `partner_semantics`, `symlink_escape`,\n  `resolved_path_toctou`, `holdout_leak`, `untrusted_checkout_execution`.\n- Deferred: none.\n- Blocked: none.\n- `graphCoverageMode`: `graphless_fallback`.\n- `searchDebt`: empty.\n- `hasSearchDebt: false`.\n\n### Candidate Coverage\n\n- The candidate set was the nine `accuracy-runner` paths. Every changed source file was read at\n  its changed lines; the two changed tests were read in full around the additions; the generated\n  `codex.d.mts.map` was checked for the expected declaration shift only.\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: none.\n- `cleanSearchProof`: every required bug class has at least one cited direct read or grep.\n\n### Ledger Rows\n\n| Id | Dimension | Bug class | Disposition |\n|----|-----------|-----------|-------------|\n| AR4B-SL-001 | correctness | field_persistence | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-002 | correctness | writer_parity | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-003 | correctness | partner_semantics | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-004 | correctness | doc_code_drift | found (AR4B-P2-001) |\n| AR4B-SL-005 | security | symlink_escape | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-006 | security | resolved_path_toctou | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-007 | security | holdout_leak | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-008 | security | untrusted_checkout_execution | ruled_out |\n| AR4B-SL-009 | traceability | doc_code_drift | found (AR4B-P2-001) |\n| AR4B-SL-010 | maintainability | doc_code_drift | found (AR4B-P2-002) |\n| AR4B-SL-011 | traceability | checklist_evidence | ruled_out |\n\n---\n\n## Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence Summary\n\n- Iterations: 3 of 3. Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. Convergence was not declared.\n- Ratios: 0.0 → 0.0 → 1.0. The two clean iterations reached the stuck threshold, so iteration 3\n  was a recovery pass at line-level doc granularity.\n- Dimension coverage: 4 of 4 (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\n\n### Coverage Summary\n\n- Correctness: iteration 1; both writers and their tests.\n- Security: iteration 2; Codex reader, containment helper, holdout guard.\n- Traceability and maintainability: iteration 3 recovery pass; README, doctor row, phase 027\n  task rows.\n\n### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- A missing `offeredAs` on either writer: ruled out by the two writer lines and their tests.\n- A partner-side command counted as an offer: ruled out by the scorer's side check.\n- A Codex link escaping the store or being opened as the link: ruled out by `resolveInside` and\n  the new test.\n- A holdout row reaching a live turn through the G2 table: ruled out by row-id comparison.\n- The A11 row contradicting the doctor code: ruled out by the checker message and the embed's\n  insert-only path.\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/helpers.mjs`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/identity.mjs` (context)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` (context)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs` (context)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md`\n\n### Cross-Reference Protocols\n\n- Core: `spec_code` partial, `checklist_evidence` partial.\n- Overlay: `skill_agent` notApplicable, `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable,\n  `feature_catalog_code` notApplicable, `playbook_capability` notApplicable.\n\n### Release Readiness\n\n`in-progress`. The verdict is PASS with advisories, but the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`\nand the packet checklist is still open, so the converged state is not claimed.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Four (accuracy-runner lineage)\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Pass: the confirming round of review pass four, on the fix range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b`, area `accuracy-runner`, run `fanout-accuracy-runner-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`, executor `cli-opencode` `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max.\\n- Reviewed scope: the nine paths in `review/review-scope-4b.txt` whose area is `accuracy-runner` — the routing-accuracy offer and runner pair, their two changed tests, the Codex session reader and its test, the Codex declaration map, and the doctor presentation row — plus the shared README that describes the pair.\\n- Inputs to this synthesis: the three iteration narratives, the three delta files, the lineage registry (2 active P2 findings), the strategy and the dashboard.\\n- Cross-area boundary: `lib/command-attach.ts`, the scorer modules, the feature docs and `score-command-transcripts.mjs` belong to `scorer-attach-confirm-4b`. This lineage read them only as context and raises no finding against them.\\n- Iteration cap: 3 of 3. The loop stopped at the cap; convergence was not declared.\\n- Operator review focus: Confirming round of review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and follow specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4b.txt: it names the scope file, the commit range, which files your lineage reviews and the checks. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Verdict: PASS.** No P0 and no P1 findings are active.\\n- **hasAdvisories: true.** Two P2 documentation drifts remain active.\\n- **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 0, P2 2.\\n- **The P1 that this round confirms is fixed.** `offeredAs` now travels from `parseOffer` through both run-log writers: the backfill at `command-offer.mjs:496` and the live turn at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1203` via `offerLineFields`. The scorer's single consumer reads the field at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1471-1476`.\\n- **The Codex containment P2 is fixed.** `resolveInside` realpaths both sides and the reader now opens `storePath` (`codex.mjs:169`). The new test proves the link path is never opened and the resolved file is (`codex.test.mjs:117-127`).\\n- **The holdout guard holds in this area.** `findRow` refuses a split-holdout row before its prompt can reach a child (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:633-634`), and the G2 fixed prompts are runner-owned ids absent from both corpora. The live-capture half of the guard is present in the sibling area at `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:206-210`.\\n- **The A11 malformed-row guidance agrees with the code.** The checker reports the cell count against the header width (`agents-md-check.cjs:776-778`), and the embed only splices missing rows (`agents-md-embed.cjs:373-410`).\\n- **The two P2s are README drift, not code drift.** The backfill paragraph still says three fields (`README.md:76`) and the runner table row lists three (`README.md:125`); the blanket \\\"every line carries four fields\\\" sentence (`README.md:65`) is false for the head-moved line written at `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183`.\\n- **Holdout hygiene:** no prompt was opened or printed. Corpus work was limited to `jq 'del(.prompt)'` id and split counts and to source-level row lookup. Holdout prompt text was never read.\\n- **Cross-runtime:** the changed Codex reader is shared; the runner's prompt and refusal logic is runtime-neutral. No live per-runtime session was captured in this lineage.\\n- **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached; no convergence event was recorded, and the packet checklist is still open.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nNo plan is required for the PASS verdict. The two P2s are advisory documentation corrections that can fold into phase 027 T012's follow-up; they do not block release.\\n\\n```json Planning Packet\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"triggerReason\\\": \\\"PASS with two advisory documentation drifts; no P0 or P1 remains.\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"counts\\\": { \\\"p0\\\": 0, \\\"p1\\\": 0, \\\"p2\\\": 2, \\\"active\\\": 2, \\\"iterations\\\": 3 },\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AR4B-P2-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"doc_code_drift\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AR4B-P2-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"doc_code_drift\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"advisory\\\": true,\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"README attribution contract\\\",\\n      \\\"files\\\": [\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\\\"],\\n      \\\"actions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Change the backfill paragraph at :76 from three fields to four and name offeredAs.\\\",\\n        \\\"Add offeredAs to the run-command-behaviour field list at :125.\\\",\\n        \\\"Qualify the every-line sentence at :65 for the head-moved line, or state the exception beside the head-moved paragraph.\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"The routing-accuracy README is the doc of record for the two writers; its field lists must match the six fields the backfill writes and the four the live turn writes.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Edit README.md:76 and :125 to name offeredAs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Edit README.md:65 to name the head-moved exception, or move the four-field statement under a completed-turn qualification.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"doc_code_drift\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"routing-accuracy README attribution section\\\",\\n    \\\"run-command-behaviour head_moved path\\\",\\n    \\\"command-offer backfill output contract\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### AR4B-P2-001 — The README still says the backfill adds three fields and lists three in the runner row\\n\\n- Severity: P2\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:76`\\n- Finding class: `doc_code_drift`\\n- Evidence: `README.md:76` says \\\"adds those three fields\\\"; `README.md:125` says `--backfill` rewrites with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered`; `README.md:188` already names `offeredAs`; `command-offer.mjs:496` and `run-command-behaviour.mjs:824` write it.\\n- Case: run `--backfill`; every output line carries `offeredAs` (pinned by `command-offer.vitest.ts:385-388`), while the paragraph and the row count three.\\n- Fix: change \\\"three\\\" to \\\"four\\\" in the backfill paragraph and add `offeredAs` to the runner table row's field list.\\n- Scope proof: the README is in the declared scope; the two code lines are the changed writers.\\n- Affected surface hints: README backfill section, runner table row, the `offeredAs` attribution contract.\\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\\n\\n### AR4B-P2-002 — The README says every run line carries four attribution fields, but a head-moved line carries none\\n\\n- Severity: P2\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:65`\\n- Finding class: `doc_code_drift`\\n- Evidence: `README.md:65` says each appended line carries four fields; `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1180-1184` appends `{ ...line, restored: false, headMoved: true }` before the offer replay and returns exit 3.\\n- Case: a turn that commits or stashes during the run sets `headMoved`; the written line has no `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` or `briefDelivered`, and the scorer reads it as `offerFieldAbsent`.\\n- Fix: qualify the sentence for a completed turn, or name the head-moved exception in the paragraph that already documents exit 3.\\n- Scope proof: the README and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both in the declared scope.\\n- Affected surface hints: head-moved run line, exit 3, attribution contract, scorer `offerFieldAbsent`.\\n- Disposition: advisory, P2.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n### P0 — none\\n\\n### P1 — none\\n\\n### P2 — advisory documentation\\n\\n1. README attribution contract (`routing-accuracy/README.md`):\\n   - `:76` — three → four, and name `offeredAs`.\\n   - `:125` — add `offeredAs` to the `--backfill` field list.\\n   - `:65` — qualify the every-line sentence for the head-moved line, or name the exception in the exit-3 paragraph.\\n\\nThese edits touch one file and no code. They can fold into the phase 027 T012 follow-up.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The README's attribution section owns four live-turn fields (`offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `briefDelivered`) and six backfill fields (the four plus `offerError` and `offerBackfilled`).\\n- The head-moved line is a partial record by construction: it is written before the replay and the restore. Any \\\"every line\\\" statement must exclude it or say what it carries.\\n- Phase 027 T012's \\\"both field lists\\\" reading should include the backfill paragraph and the runner table row, not only the top list and the output sentence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Update `README.md:76` to four fields and name `offeredAs`.\\n- Update `README.md:125` to add `offeredAs` to the backfill field list.\\n- Update `README.md:65` and the head-moved paragraph so the partial line is explicit.\\n- Re-run the README's own counts if any are asserted; no code or test change is needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Phase 027 T006/T007/T010/T012/T013/T017 are `[x]` with evidence and the code matches T006/T007/T010. T012's \\\"both field lists\\\" misses the backfill paragraph and runner row (AR4B-P2-001). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | `CHK-040` asks `RA` to name `offeredAs` in both field lists; the two lists T012 edited are correct, the backfill lists remain stale. `CHK-FIX-003`/`CHK-FIX-004` stay open with the phase. |\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-------|\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | No runtime branch in the changed docs or writers; the Codex reader is shared and tested directly. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog page describes the two changed writers. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\\n\\n### AC_COVERAGE\\n\\n`exempt`. The review target's root folder has no `acceptance-criteria.md`; the phase children hold\\ntheir own criteria, and this lineage's scope is the changed `accuracy-runner` files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Residual Codex read race.** A target replaced after `realpathSync` but before `readFileSync`\\n  remains a narrow race. The verify report's probe (a link swapped before containment) is fixed;\\n  closing the residual needs an `open` with a no-follow flag, which is outside this change.\\n- **A11 duplicate-row note.** A malformed shipped router row is reported as malformed and as\\n  missing, so an embed adds a second, well-formed copy and leaves the malformed row. The new A11\\n  row does not claim otherwise; it is an operator note, not a finding.\\n- **Sibling surfaces.** The live-capture holdout guard (`command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`), the\\n  scorer's `paired` key and `unscoredOnly`, and the feature docs are the sibling lineage's\\n  findings and are not re-reported here.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: none.\\n- Failed pivots: none.\\n- Audited overrides: none.\\n- Swept directions: none; the three iterations covered correctness, security and the\\n  traceability/maintainability recovery pass.\\n- Selected review directions: offer persistence, Codex containment, holdout guard, README and\\n  doctor row agreement.\\n- Remaining frontier: the packet checklist is still open, so traceability and maintainability are\\n  recorded as partial rather than complete.\\n- This section records breadth only. It does not change the Executive Summary, the finding\\n  registry or the verdict.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Search Ledger\\n\\n### Search Coverage\\n\\n- Required bug classes: `field_persistence`, `writer_parity`, `partner_semantics`,\\n  `doc_code_drift`, `symlink_escape`, `resolved_path_toctou`, `holdout_leak`,\\n  `untrusted_checkout_execution`, `checklist_evidence`.\\n- Covered: `doc_code_drift`, `checklist_evidence`.\\n- Ruled out: `field_persistence`, `writer_parity`, `partner_semantics`, `symlink_escape`,\\n  `resolved_path_toctou`, `holdout_leak`, `untrusted_checkout_execution`.\\n- Deferred: none.\\n- Blocked: none.\\n- `graphCoverageMode`: `graphless_fallback`.\\n- `searchDebt`: empty.\\n- `hasSearchDebt: false`.\\n\\n### Candidate Coverage\\n\\n- The candidate set was the nine `accuracy-runner` paths. Every changed source file was read at\\n  its changed lines; the two changed tests were read in full around the additions; the generated\\n  `codex.d.mts.map` was checked for the expected declaration shift only.\\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: none.\\n- `cleanSearchProof`: every required bug class has at least one cited direct read or grep.\\n\\n### Ledger Rows\\n\\n| Id | Dimension | Bug class | Disposition |\\n|----|-----------|-----------|-------------|\\n| AR4B-SL-001 | correctness | field_persistence | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-002 | correctness | writer_parity | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-003 | correctness | partner_semantics | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-004 | correctness | doc_code_drift | found (AR4B-P2-001) |\\n| AR4B-SL-005 | security | symlink_escape | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-006 | security | resolved_path_toctou | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-007 | security | holdout_leak | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-008 | security | untrusted_checkout_execution | ruled_out |\\n| AR4B-SL-009 | traceability | doc_code_drift | found (AR4B-P2-001) |\\n| AR4B-SL-010 | maintainability | doc_code_drift | found (AR4B-P2-002) |\\n| AR4B-SL-011 | traceability | checklist_evidence | ruled_out |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence Summary\\n\\n- Iterations: 3 of 3. Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. Convergence was not declared.\\n- Ratios: 0.0 → 0.0 → 1.0. The two clean iterations reached the stuck threshold, so iteration 3\\n  was a recovery pass at line-level doc granularity.\\n- Dimension coverage: 4 of 4 (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\\n\\n### Coverage Summary\\n\\n- Correctness: iteration 1; both writers and their tests.\\n- Security: iteration 2; Codex reader, containment helper, holdout guard.\\n- Traceability and maintainability: iteration 3 recovery pass; README, doctor row, phase 027\\n  task rows.\\n\\n### Ruled-Out Claims\\n\\n- A missing `offeredAs` on either writer: ruled out by the two writer lines and their tests.\\n- A partner-side command counted as an offer: ruled out by the scorer's side check.\\n- A Codex link escaping the store or being opened as the link: ruled out by `resolveInside` and\\n  the new test.\\n- A holdout row reaching a live turn through the G2 table: ruled out by row-id comparison.\\n- The A11 row contradicting the doctor code: ruled out by the checker message and the embed's\\n  insert-only path.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/codex.test.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/helpers.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/identity.mjs` (context)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` (context)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs` (context)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md`\\n\\n### Cross-Reference Protocols\\n\\n- Core: `spec_code` partial, `checklist_evidence` partial.\\n- Overlay: `skill_agent` notApplicable, `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable,\\n  `feature_catalog_code` notApplicable, `playbook_capability` notApplicable.\\n\\n### Release Readiness\\n\\n`in-progress`. The verdict is PASS with advisories, but the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`\\nand the packet checklist is still open, so the converged state is not claimed.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681357891,"end":1794681396402}}}}
